import { API_V1_VERSION } from '@/lib/api/v1/version'

export const CHANGELOG_MD = `# Changelog

> Reverse-chronological release notes for the Accounted REST API. Versions follow Stripe's dated format (\`YYYY-MM-DD\`). The current version is **\`${API_V1_VERSION}\`**.

---

## ${API_V1_VERSION} *(current)*

The first stable release of the public REST API. Six phases of development covering the full agent-native surface: authentication + discovery, invoicing vertical, transactions vertical, bookkeeping engine + suppliers + compliance check, payroll + reports + import, webhooks.

### Authentication + discovery (Phase 1)

- API key auth via \`Authorization: Bearer gnubok_sk_<random>\` (live keys) / \`gnubok_sk_test_<random>\` (test keys). 100 RPM rate limit per key.
- \`gnubok_sk_test_*\` keys: same company as a live key, every write forced into dry-run (\`X-Gnubok-Mode: test\`). There is no separate sandbox company or host.
- Scope-based authorisation per endpoint (\`invoices:read\`, \`payroll:write\`, \`webhooks:manage\`, ...).
- Discovery: \`GET /llms.txt\`, \`GET /api/v1/openapi.json\`, \`GET /.well-known/skills/index.json\`.
- Health: \`GET /api/v1/health\`.
- Response envelope: \`{ data, meta: { request_id, api_version, audit, next_cursor } }\`.
- \`X-Request-Id\` on every response; idempotency on every write.

### Invoices vertical (Phase 2)

- **Customers**: GET list + detail, POST create + bulk-create, PATCH, DELETE.
- **Invoices**: GET list + detail, POST create, PATCH, lifecycle verbs \`/mark-sent\`, \`/mark-paid\`, \`/credit\`, \`/send\`, \`/bulk-create\`. PDF download at \`/{id}/pdf\`.
- VIES validation runs on commit for EU-business customers with a VAT number.
- Mixed-rate invoices supported: per-item \`vat_rate\` overrides the header rate.
- ROT/RUT-avdrag flow and supplier-invoice fakturamodellen on the AP side.

### Transactions vertical (Phase 3)

- **Transactions**: cursor-paginated GET list + detail. Single-tx verbs \`/categorize\`, \`/uncategorize\`, \`/match-invoice\`, \`/match-supplier-invoice\`. Bulk \`/ingest\` (up to 500), \`/batch-categorize\` (up to 100).
- **Reconciliation**: \`POST /reconciliation/bank/run\`, \`GET /reconciliation/bank/status\`.
- **Reads**: \`GET /accounts\`, \`GET /fiscal-periods\`.
- All write surfaces honour strict-mode (commit fully or error with no side effects).

### Typed handles (2026-10)

- **New: \`handle\` next to the id** (2026-10-16). The resources a response returns carry a typed handle beside their id, \`<prefix>_<the UUID as 32 lowercase hex>\` (\`je\` journal entry, \`inv\` customer invoice, \`sinv\` supplier invoice, \`txn\` bank transaction, \`doc\` document, \`pop\` pending operation, and more: see Ids and typed handles on the [API overview](/docs/api)). It is the same id spelled with its type. Covered: the journal entry, invoice, supplier invoice, transaction, document, pending operation (the \`?stage=true\` 202 included), customer, supplier, company, fiscal period, employee, salary run, webhook, asset, article, dimension, inbox item, expense claim, cash account, payment order, supplier payment batch and async operation endpoints that return those resources; the spec shows \`handle\` with its pattern wherever it is added. Existing fields and their values are unchanged. Additive; the API version date is unchanged.
- **New: send a handle wherever the id goes** (2026-10-16). Path ids and body or query fields named for a resource (\`journal_entry_id\`, \`credited_invoice_id\`, \`invoice_ids\`, \`period_id\`, ...) accept the handle or the plain UUID; plain UUIDs keep working everywhere. A handle of the wrong type answers \`400 HANDLE_TYPE_MISMATCH\` (new code) with \`details.issues[]\` naming the field, the \`expected_prefix\` and the \`received_prefix\`, before anything is read. A retry that spells an id as a handle instead of the UUID is the same request to \`Idempotency-Key\`. The MCP tools accept handles in their id arguments the same way.
- **New: four more prefixes** (2026-10-16): \`aud\` audit log entry (\`GET /audit-trail\`), \`rso\` reconciliation sign-off (the account status, the sign-off history, sign-off and reopen; \`.../signoff/{signoffId}/reopen\` takes the handle in the path), \`vgap\` voucher gap explanation (\`POST /voucher-gap-explanations\`) and \`team\` team, byrå or personal (\`data.team\` on \`GET /portfolio/overview\`; \`team_id\` on \`POST /companies\` takes the handle). Additive.
- **Reserved: \`bev\` business event** (2026-10-16): the prefix of a business event, the record of what a posting meant in business terms. No endpoint returns or accepts one yet; a \`business_event_id\` field will take the handle when one does. Additive.

### Capabilities (2026-10)

- **New: \`GET /companies/{companyId}/capabilities\`** (2026-10-15): which building blocks (the modules behind the OpenAPI tags) the company can use, each with \`status\`, \`reasons\` and a \`resolution\` sentence, like Stripe account capabilities. \`active\` is usable now; \`needs_plan\` means the paid plan does not include it (on a self-hosted instance, a connector key does); \`off\` means it is turned off for this company; \`unsupported\` means it is not offered for this company, because of its country or its legal form (payroll for an enskild firma that has not said it pays salaries). \`dependency_unavailable\` marks a module that needs a module which is unsupported or off, and takes that status. The kernels (\`platform\`, \`ledger\`) are always active. Read-only: it reports the gates that exist today, and the per-company module switch arrives later. The response also carries the company's \`jurisdiction\` (\`SE\`) and \`ledger_currency\` (\`SEK\`). Additive; the API version date is unchanged.

### Retries: Idempotency-Key (2026-10)

- **\`POST /api/v1/companies\` honours \`Idempotency-Key\`** (2026-10-15). With the header, a retry with the same key and body returns the company the first call created (\`200\`, \`Idempotent-Replayed: true\`), never a second company; the same key with another body answers \`409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSE\`. The header stays optional so existing callers keep working; without it a retry after a network failure still creates a second company, so send one. **Before**, the header was ignored on this route. A dry run is never cached, so the real create may reuse the preview's key. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: a repeat that overlaps the first request with the same \`Idempotency-Key\` answers \`409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_IN_PROGRESS\`** (2026-10-15). The key is now claimed before the write runs, so two requests with one key never both run: the one that arrives while the first is still running gets \`409\` with \`Retry-After\` and changes nothing, and resending it after the first has finished replays that answer (\`Idempotent-Replayed: true\`). **Before**, both could run, which on a write that posts a verifikat meant two verifikat. A failed request (5xx, 429) still caches nothing and gives the key back; a request killed before it answered frees its key after 15 minutes. Sequential retries behave as before. MCP tools that write directly and take \`idempotency_key\` answer an overlapping repeat with the same code. The API version date is unchanged.
- **\`POST /webhook-deliveries/{id}/retry\` honours \`Idempotency-Key\`** (2026-10-15): a repeat with the same key answers the first call's \`webhook_delivery_id\` instead of queueing another delivery. The header stays optional. Before, it was ignored on this route.
- **\`x-idempotent\` corrected** (2026-10-15) on eight writes whose retry behaviour it misstated: \`DELETE /assets/{id}\`, \`DELETE /invoices/{id}\`, \`POST /reconciliation/accounts/{accountKey}/links\`, \`/residual\` and \`/signoff\`, \`POST /webhooks/{id}/rotate-secret\` (each requires \`Idempotency-Key\`), \`POST /bank-connections/{connectionId}/sync\` (lease and dedupe) and \`POST /webhooks/{id}/verify\` (already-verified short circuit) now say \`true\`. Requests and responses are unchanged.

### Transactions: ingest (2026-10)

- **Behaviour change: the \`POST /transactions/ingest\` dry-run predicts the commit row by row** (2026-10-11). It runs the same dedup decision as the commit, so it now also reports a row that matches a stored unbooked transaction from an import feed (\`skip_reason: "content_match_unbooked"\`, a new value next to \`external_id_match\` and \`content_match_booked\`). It used to read booked rows only and answer \`would_skip: false\` for a row the commit then skipped. Every item also carries \`matched_external_id\` and \`matched_transaction_id\`, and the preview adds \`would_skip_by_reason\`.
- **The commit names every skipped row** (2026-10-11): the response adds \`skipped\` (\`external_id\`, \`reason\`, \`matched_external_id\`, \`matched_transaction_id\`, in request order) and \`duplicates_by_reason\`. \`duplicates\` is unchanged and equals the length of \`skipped\`. The \`import.bank\` operation result adds \`transactions_duplicates_by_reason\`.
- **New: \`stable_external_ids\`** (2026-10-11). Set it to \`true\` when every \`external_id\` is the bank's own per-booking reference (the same booking always arrives under the same id, a different id is a different booking). A stored transaction from the same \`import_source\` under another id is then never treated as a copy of an incoming row, so identical movements on one day (several identical fees, each with its own reference) are all imported whenever they arrive. Rows from another channel (a bank file, another feed) still dedup on content. Requires the same \`import_source\` on every row. Without it nothing changes: a row identical to a stored one is skipped, and now listed in \`skipped\`.

### Collections over REST (2026-10)

- **New: collections endpoints** (2026-10-22), under \`/api/v1/companies/{companyId}\`: \`GET /collections/candidates\` (overdue invoices that could be handed over, with the checks each fails), \`GET\` and \`POST /invoices/{id}/collection\` (read the invoice's case, hand the invoice over), \`POST /invoices/{id}/collection/actions\` (pause, resume, withdraw, dispute, or answer what the provider waits for), \`GET /collections/settlements\` (what the provider collected and paid out) and the bookings \`POST /collections/payments/{paymentId}/book\` and \`POST /collections/settlements/{settlementId}/book\`. The same operations as the MCP collections tools, the same scopes. Additive.
- **New: \`400 STAGE_REQUIRED\`** (2026-10-22): the handover and the escalating case actions (approve_step, contest_dispute, confirm_not_paid, approve_legal_action) are approved only by a person in Accounted, so over REST they are sent with \`?stage=true\`; a direct call answers \`STAGE_REQUIRED\` and does nothing. Their dry runs work as usual.

### Approvals over REST: pending operations and stage mode (2026-10)

- **New: the approval door for staged writes** (2026-10-15). \`GET /pending-operations\` (cursor-paginated, \`status\` default \`pending\`, \`all\` for every status), \`GET /pending-operations/{id}\`, \`POST /pending-operations/{id}/approve\` and \`POST /pending-operations/{id}/reject\`, under \`/api/v1/companies/{companyId}\`. Scopes \`pending_operations:read\` and \`pending_operations:approve\`, as on MCP. Approve commits now and answers the committed operation; a high-risk one needs \`{"confirmed": true}\`; approving twice never commits twice (the second answers \`409 PENDING_OPERATION_NOT_PENDING\`). Both POSTs require \`Idempotency-Key\`. Additive.
- **New: \`task_state\` on every pending operation** (2026-10-15): the status in the MCP Tasks / A2A vocabulary, \`working\` (pending, committing), \`completed\` (committed), \`failed\` (the approved commit did not go through), \`cancelled\` (rejected, expired or superseded), beside the unchanged \`status\`. The MCP tool \`gnubok_list_pending_operations\` carries it too.
- **New: \`?stage=true\` on the writes agents stage over MCP** (2026-10-15, \`x-stage-supported\` in the spec): the write is staged for approval instead of committed and answers \`202\` with the pending operation. \`stage=true\` on any other endpoint answers \`400 STAGE_NOT_SUPPORTED\`, and a value other than \`true\` or \`false\` is \`400\`. Before, the parameter was ignored, so a write sent with it committed. The API version date is unchanged.
- **New: pinned previews** (2026-10-15, \`x-preview-token-supported\` in the spec). The dry run of every operation write also answers \`data.preview_token\`. Send it back in the \`Preview-Token\` header on the commit (or on \`?stage=true\`) and the commit books exactly the previewed result, or answers \`409 PREVIEW_STALE\` with the fresh preview and its token in \`error.details\` and writes nothing. The header on an endpoint without the flag, or a malformed value, is \`400\`. Without the header nothing changes; additive. Over MCP the generated write tools take the same token as \`preview_token\` when staging.

### Document signing with BankID (2026-10)

- **New: signing requests** (2026-10-25). \`POST /signing-requests\` sends an archived PDF for BankID signing: one link per signer to a page where they read the document and sign with their own BankID, mailed when they have an address (\`signers[].url\` is answered only for a signer no mail reached; the URL is the credential). The document is frozen by its SHA-256, which every signature carries. \`GET /signing-requests\` and \`GET /signing-requests/{id}\` show every signer's status and, once completed, \`signed_document_id\` (the PDF with a Signeringsbevis page) and \`evidence_document_id\` (Bevispaket.zip: the original, each BankID signature and OCSP response, a manifest), both archive documents. \`POST /signing-requests/{id}/signers/{signerId}/remind\` mails a pending signer again with a new link (once a day at most); \`POST /signing-requests/{id}/cancel\` stops an open request. Scopes \`documents:read\` and \`documents:write\`. No endpoint signs: each signer signs in person. A personnummer cannot be sent; locking a signer to one person is done in the app. MCP: \`gnubok_request_signature\` and \`gnubok_remind_signer\` stage, \`gnubok_list_signing_requests\` and \`gnubok_get_signing_request\` read.
- **New: the board signs the årsredovisning with BankID** (2026-10-25). \`POST /fiscal-periods/{id}/arsredovisning/versions/{versionId}/signing-request\` sends a locked version to its signers, one per pending slot; each BankID signature fills its slot and the last one makes the version signed. The signer's BankID name must match the slot's name (\`SIGNING_NAME_MISMATCH\`), and a version is signed one way: \`ARSREDOVISNING_SIGNING_TRACK_MIXED\` when a slot already has a signature recorded by hand. MCP: \`gnubok_request_arsredovisning_signatures\` stages.
- **Changed: \`signing_method: "bankid"\` cannot be recorded by hand** (2026-10-25). \`PATCH /fiscal-periods/{id}/arsredovisning/signatures/{signatureId}\` answers \`422 SIGNING_METHOD_RESERVED\` for it: \`bankid\` now means a signature made with BankID in Accounted, with the signature behind it. A BankID signature made in another service is \`advanced_e_signature\`. A slot covered by a BankID signing request takes no evidence by hand (\`409 ARSREDOVISNING_SIGNING_TRACK_MIXED\`).
- **New: the revisor in the årsredovisning's signer roster** (2026-10-27). \`POST /fiscal-periods/{id}/arsredovisning/signatures\` takes the roles \`Auktoriserad revisor\`, \`Godkänd revisor\` and \`Huvudansvarig revisor\`: that slot holds the revisorspåteckning (ABL 9 kap. 28 §), recorded by hand with \`PATCH .../signatures/{signatureId}\` once the revisionsberättelse is given and the whole board has signed, in the board's medium: \`advanced_e_signature\` on a version the board signed electronically (BankID included; the board's signing request covers the board's slots only), \`paper_original\` on a paper original. The compliance profile takes \`auditor_firm_name\` (the elected revisionsbolag) and \`auditor_opinion\` (what the revisionsberättelse says); both are frozen on the revisor's slot as it is signed, so a signed or filed version keeps the påteckning it was given. A revisor role cannot sign the fastställelseintyg. Additive; the API version date is unchanged.
- **New webhooks** (2026-10-25): \`signing.signer_signed\`, \`signing.declined\` and \`signing.completed\`. Payloads carry ids, positions and times, never names, addresses or personnummer. Additive; the API version date is unchanged.
- **Changed: signing is part of the paid plan** (2026-10-26). \`POST /signing-requests\` and the årsredovisning \`signing-request\` answer \`403 SIGNING_CAPABILITY_BLOCKED\` for a company with neither a paid plan nor a trial; \`SIGNING_UNAVAILABLE\` now means signing is not switched on for that company. Reading, reminding and cancelling a request already sent are unchanged, and every signer with an email now gets the signed PDF when the last one signs.

### Inbox, transactions and documents (2026-10)

- **Behaviour change: \`GET /inbox-items\` reads one definition of an open item** (2026-11-01). \`processed\` is true, and \`unprocessed_only=true\` leaves the item out, also when Arkiv took it or when a verifikat holds its document, stamp or not. A document on a reversed verifikat is not held: its item is open again. A page of \`unprocessed_only=true\` can run short with a \`next_cursor\` to go on from. Same answer as \`gnubok_list_inbox_items\`, the Inkorg and the counts.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /inbox-items/{id}/convert\` refuses a second booking of the purchase** (2026-11-01). Where registering posts a verifikat, an item a live verifikat books already, by its stamp or because that verifikat holds its document, answers \`409 INBOX_ITEM_ALREADY_BOOKED\` with \`details.journal_entry_id\`, and nothing is registered. Registering with no verifikat (kontantmetoden, a company that defers booking) is unchanged. The same document on a live verifikat now also stops \`POST /expense-claims\` and the Inkorg's direct booking. The supplier card takes the document's bank details once the invoice exists, no longer before a refusal.
- **New: \`POST /inbox-items\`, the partner door into the Inkorg** (2026-10-15, scope \`documents:write\`). A partner delivering documents on a company's behalf (a digital mailbox, a scanning service) sends one PDF or image per call as \`multipart/form-data\`, with optional \`kind_hint\` (\`supplier_invoice\` | \`receipt\`), \`external_ref\` (your id, 1-200 chars), \`sender_name\`, \`sender_org_number\`, \`subject\`, \`message\` and \`received_at\`. It takes the path of a person's upload: archived, deduplicated on content, read by extraction, and filed among the Inkorg's open items for a person or a granted agent to book. **It books nothing.** \`201\` answers \`inbox_item_id\`, \`document_id\`, \`deduplicated\` and \`arrival_id\`; a repeated \`external_ref\` (or a file already in the Inkorg) answers \`200\` with the existing item and \`deduplicated: true\`, and the same \`external_ref\` with another file answers \`409 INBOX_DELIVERY_REF_CONFLICT\`. \`Idempotency-Key\` is required. A mailbox partner that today calls \`POST /supplier-invoices\` (which registers and books on arrival) should deliver here instead.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /transactions/{id}/match-batch\` refuses a transaction in a foreign currency** (2026-11-01), with \`400 BATCH_FOREIGN_CURRENCY\` (\`details.currency\`), the dry run included, as \`POST /transactions/bulk-book\` does. **Before**, the transaction's foreign figure was booked as kronor on both legs: 1 000 EUR became Dr 1932 1 000 / Cr 1510 1 000 on an invoice worth 11 300 kr, and the entry balanced. Match such a transaction to one invoice at a time (\`match-invoice\`, \`match-supplier-invoice\`). A SEK transaction against foreign invoices works as before; the dry run now also answers the \`400 BATCH_FX_DEVIATION_TOO_LARGE\` the commit would. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /transactions/{id}/match-supplier-invoice\` reads a row in another currency against the remaining balance** (2026-11-01), at Riksbanken's rate on the payment date, the invoice's own rate when there is none. Short by more than 2 % it is a part payment: \`status\` \`partially_paid\`, 2440 cleared by that part and the kursdifferens booked on it. Above the balance by more than 10 % it answers \`400 MATCH_SI_AMOUNT_EXCEEDS_REMAINING\`. Anything between settles the balance, the difference on 3960/7960, as before: a card rate runs a few percent over the mid rate. Under kontantmetoden a part payment of a never-booked invoice answers \`400 MATCH_SI_CASH_FX_UNSUPPORTED\`. **Before**, any amount settled the whole balance: half a payment closed the debt and booked the rest as a gain, and under kontantmetoden booked the whole invoice at half its value. With neither rate the match answers \`400 SI_FX_RATE_MISSING\`. The API version date is unchanged.
- **A full settlement of a foreign invoice clears what the ledger carries** (2026-11-01). \`match-invoice\`, \`match-supplier-invoice\`, \`match-batch\` and \`POST /invoices/{id}/mark-paid\` clear what the invoice's own vouchers left on 1510 or 2440, not the balance at the rate, so a paid invoice leaves no öre on the account, and the difference to the kronor that moved lands on 3960/7960. On \`mark-paid\`, \`exchange_rate_difference\` stays measured from the booked rate: the bank takes that figure plus the difference and the gap to the ledger is the FX line, and custom \`lines\` that clear what 1510 carries pay the whole remainder. When the vouchers cannot say (a verifikat shared with another invoice, none linked) the rate clears, as before. Foreign amounts round one way everywhere: on the written decimals, half away from zero, the sign outside the amount, so \`*_sek\` of a credit note is minus the invoice's and a preview shows the öre the commit books. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /transactions/{id}/match-invoice\` refuses a transaction that is already booked or ignored** (#58, 2026-11-01). When the transaction's pointer or a \`bank_line\` voucher link names a posted verifikat, or it is linked to an existing verifikat, the match answers \`409 MATCH_INVOICE_TX_ALREADY_BOOKED\` and writes nothing; \`details\` names the verifikat (\`journal_entry_id\`, \`voucher\`, \`via\`: \`pointer\`, \`link\`, \`reconciliation\`, or \`concurrent\` when another booking took the transaction first) and says in \`undo\` how the transaction opens again: \`uncategorize\` (\`POST /transactions/{id}/uncategorize\`), \`unlink\` (the reconciliation unlink: the verifikat stays posted) or \`reverse_voucher\` (a storno of the verifikat, which releases every transaction on it). An ignored transaction answers \`409 BANK_ROW_IGNORED\`. **Before**, a categorized transaction had its verifikat reversed without being asked, a transaction linked to an existing verifikat kept that verifikat posted beside the payment, and one booked only through voucher links got a second verifikat, so the bank account was debited twice; an ignored transaction answered 500 with the payment already posted and the invoice paid. Nothing else about a successful match changes. On the way: an invoice with an active credit note answers \`MATCH_INVOICE_CREDIT_NOTE\`, a pointer at a verifikat no longer posted books instead of answering \`CANNOT_REVERSE_NON_POSTED\`, and a match that stops after the payment verifikat posted cancels it and undoes its own writes. \`POST /transactions/{id}/match-batch\` and \`POST /transactions/bulk-book\` refuse the same rows, the dry run included. \`POST /reconciliation/accounts/{accountKey}/links\` and \`POST /transactions/{id}/link-journal-entry\` refuse a verifikat that is an opening balance or a storno (\`ENTRY_NOT_OPEN\`, \`LINK_TX_JE_NOT_BANK_MOVEMENT\`). The API version date is unchanged. A failed read of the transaction answers \`503 BANK_ROW_READ_FAILED\` on this door and on \`match-supplier-invoice\`, not the booked refusal: nothing was booked, so retry.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /transactions/{id}/match-supplier-invoice\` refuses a transaction that is already booked** (#58, 2026-10-28). When the transaction's pointer or a \`bank_line\` voucher link names a posted verifikat (its own categorization, a bulk-book samlingsverifikat, a split, an earlier batch match) or it is linked to an existing verifikat, the match answers \`409 MATCH_SI_TX_ALREADY_BOOKED\` and writes nothing; \`details\` names the verifikat (\`journal_entry_id\`, \`voucher\`, \`via\`: \`pointer\`, \`link\`, \`reconciliation\`, or \`concurrent\` when another booking took the transaction first) and says in \`storno_allowed\` whether it is the transaction's own categorization. Only then may the request be resent with the new body field \`storno_existing: true\`, which reverses that verifikat (storno) after every other check has passed and books the payment. **Before**, a categorized transaction had its verifikat reversed without being asked, a transaction linked to an existing verifikat was re-pointed to the payment, and one booked only through voucher links got a second verifikat, so the bank account was credited twice. The endpoint now books through the dashboard match's own code, so a failure to create the payment verifikat answers \`MATCH_SI_JE_FAILED\` (was \`MATCH_SI_RECORD_PAYMENT_FAILED\`), and a match that stops after the verifikat posted (a concurrent booking of the transaction or settlement of the invoice, a payment row that cannot be recorded) cancels it and undoes its own writes instead of leaving it posted. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: categorize, batch-categorize and bulk-book also refuse a row a samlingsverifikat already holds** (issue #101, 2026-10-26). When a posted verifikat entered outside the feed (\`source_type\` \`manual\`, or \`import\` on a payment provider's account such as 1686) books the transaction's settlement account in its direction, is dated the transaction's day (bank accounts 1910-1949) or between that day and the end of the next month (other accounts), and still has at least the transaction's amount that no transaction is linked to, the booking answers \`409 TRANSACTION_BOOK_POSSIBLE_DUPLICATE\` with that verifikat in \`details.candidate\` and the new \`details.candidate.covering\` (\`booked\`, \`held\`, \`unlinked\`, kronor). Link the transaction to it (\`POST /transactions/{id}/link-journal-entry\`) or ignore it; book it anyway only when it is not part of that verifikat, with \`force: true\` and \`expected_duplicate_journal_entry_id\`, as for the other candidates. **Before**, such a row booked a second verifikat for a sale the samlingsverifikat already held. Non-SEK rows and rows without a cash account are not checked. No field was removed, and the API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /documents\` refuses a dry run** (2026-10-15). The endpoint is not dry-runnable, but a live key sending \`?dry_run=true\` or \`X-Dry-Run: true\` had its file archived for real (the archive is WORM, so it could not be taken back) while it believed it previewed. It now answers \`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\` (\`details.field: "dry_run"\`) and stores nothing. Test keys are refused as before.
- **Fix: \`503 EXTENSION_DISABLED\` names no feature it is not about** (2026-10-15). Its message said the Skatteverket integration was off, also when bank sync or the Inkorg was. It now reads "This feature is not enabled on this installation." (sv "Funktionen är inte aktiverad i den här installationen."), and \`details.extension\` names the feature (\`enable-banking\`, \`invoice-inbox\`, \`skatteverket\`). The code and status are unchanged.
- **Fix: a resent multipart upload replays under its \`Idempotency-Key\`** (2026-10-15). The key's request hash covered the raw multipart text, and every client encodes a fresh boundary per request, so a resend of \`POST /documents\` with the same key and file answered \`409 IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSE\` instead of the first answer. Multipart bodies are now compared by their parts (each text value, and each file's name, type, size and SHA-256). JSON bodies are compared as before.
- **Behaviour change: reverse charge on \`POST /inbox-items/{id}/convert\`** (2026-10-13): the convert applies the reverse-charge rules of \`POST /supplier-invoices\`. \`reverse_charge: true\` now sets \`vat_treatment\` to \`reverse_charge\`, registers the net as the payable (\`total\`, \`remaining_amount\`) and refuses a line with a \`vat_rate\` other than 0 with \`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\` (\`details.field\` names the line). An EU or non-EU supplier without \`reverse_charge\` defaults to reverse charge, as on \`POST /supplier-invoices\`; send \`reverse_charge: false\` for a foreign supplier that charged its own or no VAT. **Before**, the convert kept \`vat_treatment\` at \`standard_25\`, priced an omitted line rate at 25 % and registered net plus VAT as the payable while the registration verifikat credited 2440 with the net, so the invoice could never settle cleanly. Invoices already registered are not touched; the API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: \`GET /transactions?status=booked|unbooked\` follows every anchor to a verifikat** (2026-10-13): \`status=unbooked\` is now the work queue, the rows the period-lock guard, the VAT close check and the MCP list count: not ignored, not triaged as private (\`is_business\` false), and anchored to no verifikat. \`status=booked\` is every row anchored to a verifikat: the \`journal_entry_id\` pointer, a bulk booking or split (one verifikat for several rows, or one row over several verifikat) and a batch allocation against invoices, which keep \`journal_entry_id\` null. **Before**, both read \`journal_entry_id\` alone, so an ignored row and a bulk-booked or allocation-settled row were listed as unbooked and missing from \`status=booked\`; an integration that booked the unbooked list could book them again. Without \`status\` every row is listed, as before. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /documents/{id}/link\` runs the same link rules as the app and the MCP tools** (2026-10-13): a document already linked to another verifikat answers \`409 DOC_LINK_ALREADY_LINKED\` whatever that verifikat's status (posted, draft or reversed), with \`details.current_journal_entry_id\` and \`details.current_journal_entry_status\`, and so does a change of a line already set; the dry run refuses the same, and refuses a verifikat in a closed or locked period with \`PERIOD_LOCKED\`. **Before**, only a posted holder was refused, as \`409 CONFLICT\`, and a draft or reversed holder or a locked period passed the dry run and then failed live. The invoice-inbox item that carries the document is now marked handled whether or not \`inbox_item_id\` is sent, and an \`inbox_item_id\` that does not carry the document is no longer stamped (it used to stamp any inbox item of the company). A \`journal_entry_line_id\` that is not a line of \`journal_entry_id\` is \`404 NOT_FOUND\`, as before. The API version date is unchanged.

### Transactions: revenue accounts of a bank row (2026-11)

- **Behaviour change: a sale on a category books the revenue account an invoice books** (2026-11-01). \`POST /transactions/{id}/categorize\` and \`/batch-categorize\`: \`income_products\` at \`export\` or \`reverse_charge\` books 3105 or 3108, the goods accounts in ruta 36 and 35, where it booked the services accounts 3305 and 3308. An exempt sale of an enskild firma or ideell förening books 3100, where it booked 3004: same ruta and NE line. \`income_other\` stays on 3999.

### Transactions: hard blocks (2026-10)

- **Behaviour change: a booking a hard block matches is booked only by a person, from its review** (#130, 2026-10-30). An owner or admin adds hard blocks in the app (Regler, Spärrar): accounts, a counterparty, an amount from in SEK and a VAT treatment, any mix; a booking of a bank row matches when every criterion the block sets holds. A key never books such a booking directly: \`POST /transactions/{id}/categorize\` stages it for a person and answers \`202\` with the pending operation (\`staged_because: BOOKING_REVIEW_REQUIRED\`), or refuses it with \`409 BOOKING_REVIEW_REQUIRED\` when it names a template by id; \`batch-categorize\` skips the matched items with that code; \`bulk-book\` refuses a samlingsverifikat with a matched row (\`409 BOOKING_REVIEW_BULK_REFUSED\`, \`details.transaction_ids\`), also for a person, who books such a row on its own. The MCP categorize tool stages as always. \`POST /pending-operations/{id}/approve\` refuses a matched booking from a key with \`BOOKING_REVIEW_WEB_ONLY\` and leaves it pending; rules for automatic booking do not apply to it. Blocks are set and archived in the app only. Storno, rättelse and imports are never matched. A company without blocks books as before.
- **Behaviour change: hard blocks also hold supplier invoices and Inkorg documents** (#145, 2026-10-31). A supplier invoice's registration verifikat, the verifikat a kontantmetoden payment books the purchase with, and an Inkorg document booked without a bank row are judged like a bank row: the supplier (or the document's seller) is the counterparty and the invoice total in SEK the amount. A key never posts such a booking: \`POST /supplier-invoices\`, \`POST /inbox-items/{id}/convert\`, \`POST /supplier-invoices/{id}/book\`, \`POST /supplier-invoices/{id}/mark-paid\` and \`POST /transactions/{id}/match-supplier-invoice\` (kontantmetoden) answer \`409 BOOKING_REVIEW_REQUIRED\` and book nothing (a refused registration has drawn its ankomstnummer, as any refusal of the engine does); a person registers it in the app. A bank payment order's own debit no longer settles an unbooked (kontantmetoden or deferred) invoice a block may hold: it stays a suggestion for a person. \`POST /pending-operations/{id}/approve\` refuses a matched \`create_supplier_invoice_from_inbox\` with \`BOOKING_REVIEW_WEB_ONLY\` and leaves it pending, rules for automatic booking do not apply to it, and any approval the database refuses for a block now leaves the operation pending instead of rejected. Payments of registered invoices, credit notes, customer invoices and utlägg are not judged.

### Supplier invoices: attest levels (2026-10)

- **New: attest limits per person and two attesters from an amount** (#135, 2026-10-30). \`PUT /supplier-invoices/attest-policy\` takes \`two_step_from_sek\` (from that SEK total two different attesters must approve; \`null\` = one is enough) and \`limits\` (\`[{ user_id, max_amount_sek }]\`, the highest SEK total each attester's approval covers; \`null\` = no limit; it replaces every limit). Both are optional: left out, they stay as they are. \`GET\` answers them, each attester with \`limit_sek\`. With the policy on, below the two-step amount one approval by an attester whose limit covers the invoice attests it; at or above it two different attesters must approve, at least one with a covering limit, in any order. New refusals: \`400 ATTEST_POLICY_TWO_STEP_NEEDS_TWO\` and \`400 ATTEST_LIMIT_NOT_ATTESTER\` on the policy, and \`403 ATTEST_LIMIT_EXCEEDED\` on \`POST /supplier-invoices/{id}/approve\` (\`details.reason\` \`limit\` or \`key_limit\`, with \`details.limit_sek\` and \`details.amount_sek\`). With levels on (a limit or a two-step amount), an attest through an API key is capped by the lower of the key user's limit and the key's unattended ceiling. \`GET /supplier-invoices/{id}/attestations\` adds \`amount_sek\`, \`steps\`, \`approvals_needed\`, \`needs_covering\`, each \`remaining\` attester's \`limit_sek\` and each decision's \`step\`; \`remaining\` names only those whose approval would move the invoice on. A company without limits or a two-step amount attests as before.

### Supplier invoices: EU goods (2026-10)

- **New: \`reverse_charge_kind\` on a supplier invoice** (crm#1323, 2026-10-19): \`POST /supplier-invoices\` and \`POST /inbox-items/{id}/convert\` accept \`reverse_charge_kind\` (\`eu_goods\` | \`eu_services\`) for a reverse-charge invoice from a supplier in another EU country. \`eu_goods\` books the basis pair on 4515 (momsdeklaration ruta 20) / 4598 instead of 4535 (ruta 21); the fiktiv moms on 2645 / 2614 is the same, and the credit note and the kontantmetoden entries follow it. \`GET /supplier-invoices/{id}\` returns it (\`null\` books services). Sent without reverse charge or for a supplier that is not \`eu_business\` it answers \`400 SI_CREATE_INVALID_INPUT\`. Additive: nothing changes for a request without it.
- **Fix: a privately paid reverse-charge invoice registers** (crm#1377, 2026-10-22): \`POST /supplier-invoices\` with \`paid_with_private_funds: true\` and reverse charge (an EU or non-EU supplier's service bought on a private card) answered \`400 SI_CREATE_INVALID_INPUT\`. It now books the utlägg verifikat with the same fiktiv moms 2645 / 26x4 and basis pair 45xx / 4598 the registration would, and the payer's claim is the net the supplier invoiced. Lines must still carry \`vat_rate\` 0. Nothing changes for any other request.
- **Behaviour change: \`400 SI_CREATE_INVALID_INPUT\` names its rule** (#96, 2026-10-23): \`POST /supplier-invoices\` and \`POST /inbox-items/{id}/convert\` send a stable \`details.reason\` (\`reverse_charge_kind_without_reverse_charge\`, \`reverse_charge_kind_not_eu_supplier\`, \`inbox_item_requires_private_payment\`, \`inbox_item_not_found\`, \`inbox_item_already_booked\`, \`document_unavailable\`, \`document_already_used\`, \`accrual_with_private_payment\`, \`accrual_requires_accrual_method\`, \`vat_on_non_vat_registered\`, or \`expense_claim_lines_invalid\` with \`details.detail\`), and \`message\` / \`message_en\` are that rule's sentence. **Before**, \`details.reason\` was a free English sentence and both messages were the same for every refusal. A client that matched the old sentence matches the code instead. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: under kontantmetoden an EU goods invoice is booked at registration** (#73, 2026-10-22). ML 2023:200 7 kap. 26 and 40 §§ put the reverse-charge moms of an EU goods acquisition in the period the invoice is issued, whatever the buyer's accounting method. \`POST /supplier-invoices\` and \`POST /inbox-items/{id}/convert\` with \`reverse_charge_kind: "eu_goods"\` from a kontantmetoden company now post the registration verifikat on the invoice date (cost, 4515 / 4598, 2645 / 2614, credit 2440) and return \`registration_journal_entry_id\`; the dry run says \`would_create_registration_journal_entry: true\`, and an invoice date in a locked period answers \`PERIOD_LOCKED\`. Its payment then clears 2440, as under faktureringsmetoden. **Before**, nothing was posted until the payment, which booked the moms in the payment's period. EU services and every other kontantmetoden invoice are unchanged. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: an EU goods registration is dated no later than the 15th of the month after delivery** (#93, 2026-10-23). ML 2023:200 7 kap. 26 and 40 §§ put the reverse-charge moms of an EU goods acquisition in the period the invoice is issued, but at the latest in the period holding the 15th of the month after the delivery month. \`POST /supplier-invoices\`, \`POST /inbox-items/{id}/convert\` and \`POST /supplier-invoices/{id}/book\` for an invoice with \`reverse_charge_kind: "eu_goods"\` and a \`delivery_date\` now date the registration verifikat on that 15th when the invoice date is later, under both accounting methods, and check the period lock on that date (\`PERIOD_LOCKED\`; the Bokför step also returns \`details.entry_date\`). **Before**, the verifikat was always dated on the invoice date, so a late invoice reported the moms in a later period. Without \`delivery_date\`, and for every other invoice, nothing changes. The API version date is unchanged.

### Expense claims (2026-10)

- **Reverse charge on an utlägg** (crm#1028, 2026-10-09): \`POST /expense-claims\` accepts \`reverse_charge\` (\`eu_services\` | \`non_eu_services\`) for a service under huvudregeln (SaaS, licences, ads, consulting) from a seller abroad that charged no VAT. Hotel, restaurant, taxi, travel and event costs abroad are taxed where performed and take no \`reverse_charge\`. The verifikat then also carries the fiktiv moms 2645 D / 2614 K on the SEK amount and the basis pair 4535 (ruta 21) or 4531 (ruta 22) D / 4598 K, left out when \`expense_account\` reports that ruta itself. It needs \`vat_amount\` 0, no \`lines\` and an \`expense_account\` that reports no other box (\`400\` otherwise). Additive: nothing changes for a request without it.

### Reports and compliance (2026-10)

- **Behaviour change: \`GET /compliance/check?type=vat_close\` compares each VAT rate with the previous period** (2026-10-28). \`details.sanity.ratios.rate_shares\` is new: \`{ current, previous }\`, each \`{ "25", "12", "6" }\`, the rate's share in percent of the taxable base derived from output VAT (ruta 10/11/12 divided by the rate), or \`null\` when the period has no sales, a rate is negative, or (\`previous\`) the previous period was not read. A new anomaly kind, \`rate_share_shift\`, fires once per rate whose share moved at least 15 percentage points while its base moved at least max(25 000 kr, 10 % of the larger total); its \`current\` and \`previous\` are shares in percent, \`delta_pct\` the change in percentage points, and \`current_base\` and \`previous_base\` (new fields) the rate's base in kronor. \`output_vat_ratio_drift\` is no longer emitted: ruta 10 / ruta 05 moved with the sales mix of any company selling at more than one rate, and could not see 12 % or 6 %. \`revenue_drop\` and \`revenue_spike\` keep their thresholds but stay quiet when both periods' ruta 05 is below 25 000 kr. \`ratios.output_vat_ratio_25\`, \`_12\` and \`_6\` are deprecated and still returned unchanged; read \`rate_shares\`. The thresholds are a first proposal, to be calibrated against real declarations. \`sanity\` stays advisory: \`ready\` is unchanged. The MCP tool \`gnubok_vat_close_check\` returns the same \`sanity\`. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: a year left unclosed opens the next on its closing account** (2026-10-24): when a year's opening balance is derived from history, an earlier year that ended without a booked resultatavslut is read as closed, so its result opens on 2099 (enskild firma 2010, ideell förening 2069) and the later balance sheets, saldobalans and huvudbok balance. Booking the real closing replaces it. \`imbalance_diagnosis\` on \`GET /reports/balance-sheet\` no longer carries \`untransferred_results\`.
- **Behaviour change: \`GET /compliance/check?type=vat_close\` returns the rutor as filed** (2026-10-13): \`details.rutor\` is the momsdeklaration Skatteverket receives, box for box and signed (a box whose credit notes exceed its sales is negative, as it is in the filing). Before, every box but ruta 49 was an absolute value and ruta 05 also summed a fixed list of class 3 accounts (3041-3078, 3106, ...) the filing leaves out. A class 3 account in no ruta is reported by the \`REVENUE_ACCOUNT_WITHOUT_RUTA\` finding instead. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Docs fix: \`GET /reports/trial-balance\` rows** (2026-10-13): the reference described \`account\`, \`opening_balance\` and \`closing_balance\`, fields the response never had. It now documents what is returned: \`account_number\`, \`account_name\`, \`account_class\` and the opening, period and closing debit and credit per account, each side gross (the balance is \`closing_debit - closing_credit\`). The response itself is unchanged.

### Fiscal periods and journal entries (2026-10)

- **New: \`owned_by\` on reverse and correct** (2026-10-18). \`POST /journal-entries/{id}/reverse\` and \`/correct\`, live and dry run, answer \`owned_by\`: the invoice, credit note, supplier invoice, periodisering, asset or payroll run the verifikat books, with its own \`action\`, \`action_href\`, the MCP \`tool\` that does it and a one-line \`hint_sv\` / \`hint_en\`, or \`null\`. The storno or correction is posted exactly as before; that object does not follow it, so a credit is usually the better call. Additive field, the API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: one opening balance per fiscal year on every door** (2026-10-13). A year counts as having its IB when it points at one or holds any posted \`source_type=opening_balance\` verifikat, including one booked through the agent's voucher tool or left by a replaced SIE import, which no pointer named. \`POST /fiscal-periods/{id}/opening-balances\` answers \`409 CONFLICT\` (\`details.reason\` \`opening_balance_already_posted\`, now with \`details.existing_entry_id\`) and posts nothing; a reversed (stornoed) IB no longer blocks it. \`POST /fiscal-periods/{id}/opening-balances/manual\` answers \`409 OB_PERIOD_ALREADY_HAS_BALANCES\` for such a year, dry run included, where it used to post a second IB. \`POST /fiscal-periods/{id}/year-end\` and \`GET /compliance/check?type=year_end_readiness\` report \`NEXT_PERIOD_HAS_IB\` for it, before anything is posted. An IB booked as a voucher now also points its year at itself, so \`POST /opening-balances/correct\` works on it. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: a storno is dated inside the original's fiscal year** (2026-10-13). \`POST /journal-entries/{id}/reverse\` defaults \`reversal_date\` to the original entry's date (it was today), as the app and the agent tools already did. The storno is numbered in the original's series and booked into the original's fiscal year, so a \`reversal_date\` outside that year answers \`400 ENTRY_DATE_OUTSIDE_FISCAL_PERIOD\`; it used to be posted dated in the other year, counted in one year by the trial balance and in another by the VAT report. A locked or closed year, or a date on or before the company lock date, answers \`PERIOD_LOCKED\` (\`details.reason\`) before any voucher number is drawn, live and dry run alike; the lock used to be checked on today's period, and a locked original year failed at the database after using up a voucher number. The same check runs on \`POST /journal-entries/{id}/correct\` before its storno. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: a voucher gap check that cannot run blocks year-end** (2026-10-13). \`GET /compliance/check?type=year_end_readiness\` and \`POST /fiscal-periods/{id}/year-end\` report a blocker when the gap detection or the gap explanations cannot be read, where the series used to be skipped and the year could close past an unexplained gap. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: voucher gap explanations are checked once, the same way, and are write-once** (2026-10-13). \`POST /voucher-gap-explanations\` takes an \`explanation\` of 1-500 characters after trimming (it accepted 2000, and 501-2000 then failed in the database) and answers \`409 VOUCHER_GAP_ALREADY_EXPLAINED\` for a gap that already has one, dry run included; a saved explanation is never overwritten. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /imports/sie\` reads its \`options\` through the import job's own schema** (2026-10-13), the one the dashboard and the agent tools use. Vouchers the file gives no series now go to series B, as on the dashboard (this endpoint defaulted \`voucherSeries\` to A); \`voucherSeries\` and \`openingBalanceSeries\` take up to 16 characters (was 2); \`markImportedNoDocRequired\` is accepted. Every other default is unchanged (\`createFiscalPeriod\`, \`importOpeningBalances\`, \`importTransactions\` and \`updateAccountNames\` true), and an unknown key is still \`400\`. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Docs: the year-end flow is one call** (2026-10-13). The reference pages for \`/lock\`, \`/year-end\`, \`/close\` and \`/opening-balances\` prescribed lock, then year-end, then close, which fails: \`POST /fiscal-periods/{id}/year-end\` runs on an unlocked period and locks it, closes it and generates the next year's IB itself. \`/close\` is a recovery path and \`/lock\` is for interim locks. The year-end page now says to poll \`GET /api/v1/operations/{id}\` or subscribe to \`period.year_closed\` (\`operation.completed\` is not a deliverable webhook), and its 202 example shows \`status: "queued"\`, as the response does. Nothing on the wire changed.

### API keys: inspect a key's grant (2026-10)

- **Behaviour change: an archived company answers \`404\`** (2026-11-01). A call naming a company that has been archived now answers \`404 NOT_FOUND\`, reads and writes alike, as an unknown company does and as the MCP server and \`GET /api/events\` already did. \`GET /companies\` and \`GET /api-key\` left such a company out before, but it stayed reachable by id. The company's data is kept; only the door is closed.
- **A refused write names why** (2026-11-01). A write refused because the membership is a viewer, or the key has read-only access to the company, is \`403 FORBIDDEN\` with \`error.details.code\` \`ROLE_READ_ONLY\` or \`CONNECTION_READ_ONLY\`, as before. The MCP server now carries the same \`details.code\` on its error. Additive.
- **OAuth connections are named as their client** (2026-11-01). Everything a key from the OAuth sign-in writes through the REST API now records the actor \`mcp_oauth\` with the client's name (\`Claude (Anthropic)\`), as the MCP server does: \`committed_actor_*\` on a verifikat, \`actor_type\` and \`actor_label\` on a pending operation. They recorded \`api_key\` with the reserved key name. Rows already written keep what they carry.

- **\`GET /api/v1/api-key\`** (2026-10-07): returns the calling key's \`mode\` (\`live\` | \`test\`), its \`scopes\`, \`company_access\` (\`all_memberships\` or \`allowlist\`) and every company it reaches with \`role\`, \`access\` (\`read_write\` | \`read_only\`) and \`read_only_code\` (\`ROLE_READ_ONLY\` | \`CONNECTION_READ_ONLY\`, the codes a refused write answers with). Any valid key may call it, whatever its scopes, including keys issued through MCP OAuth; no key gives \`401\`. Check a key when a customer connects it instead of waiting for the first \`403\`: a document upload to company X needs \`documents:write\` in \`scopes\`, X with \`access\` \`read_write\`, and \`mode\` \`live\` (a test key gets \`403 TEST_KEY_WRITE_BLOCKED\` on uploads, which cannot be dry-run). Additive.
- The reference pages said live keys start \`gnubok_sk_live_\`. They start \`gnubok_sk_\` followed directly by the random part; only test keys carry an infix (\`gnubok_sk_test_\`). The OpenAPI \`bearerFormat\` now says the same.

### Fiscal years (2026-11)

- **Behaviour change: a year has ended the day after its last day** (2026-11-01). On the last day itself \`POST /fiscal-periods/{id}/year-end\` and \`GET /compliance/check?type=year_end_readiness\` report \`PERIOD_NOT_ENDED\`, and \`POST /fiscal-periods/{id}/close-external\` answers \`409 FISCAL_PERIOD_CLOSE_EXTERNAL_NOT_ENDED\`, as the VAT and annual report doors already did.
- **Behaviour change: an enskild firma keeps the calendar year on create and import** (2026-11-01). \`POST /fiscal-periods\` answers \`400 FISCAL_PERIOD_ENSKILD_FIRMA_CALENDAR_YEAR\` for a year not ending on 31 December, or a later year not starting on 1 January, as \`PATCH\` did; an SIE import with such a year is refused.
- **Fixed: \`exceeds_18_months\` on \`GET /fiscal-periods\` counts like the doors that refuse a year**: a year starting on the last of a month is over the cap by that day.
- **Behaviour change: a next year that cannot be created stops the year-end before anything is posted** (2026-11-01). \`POST /fiscal-periods/{id}/year-end\` and \`GET /compliance/check?type=year_end_readiness\` report \`NEXT_PERIOD_NOT_CALENDAR_YEAR\` for an enskild firma whose year does not end on 31 December, and \`NEXT_PERIOD_OVERLAPS\` when a later year starts inside the twelve months after this one: create the shorter year between them first. The close used to post its closing entry and then fail.
- **Fixed: a yearly VAT period follows the recorded räkenskapsår.** The \`tax_period\`, dates and due date on the filing record are the recorded year's when \`fiscal_year_start_month\` is out of step with it, \`period_start\` is that year's own first day also when it runs longer or shorter than twelve months, and the report without \`fiscal_period_id\` reads the year that has started when two end in one calendar year. An enskild firma keeps the calendar year as its key, as its deadline does.

### Recording a payment by hand (2026-11)

- **Behaviour change: \`POST /supplier-invoices/{id}/mark-paid\` books through the dashboard's payment path, and the dashboard through the same rules** (2026-11-01). An amount above what the invoice still owes answers \`400 MATCH_SI_AMOUNT_EXCEEDS_REMAINING\` with \`details.remaining_amount\` and \`details.excess\` (it was \`VALIDATION_ERROR\`). A credit note answers \`400 SI_PAID_NOT_PAYABLE\` with \`details.reason\` \`credit_note\` (it was \`VALIDATION_ERROR\`). A payment row that cannot be written, or a lost race, now cancels the payment voucher and documents its number as a gap; it used to storno it, or leave the invoice paid with no row. Under dry-run edited \`lines\` are checked too, and \`warnings\` carries the Bokför step's warnings when the registration was booked first.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /invoices/{id}/mark-paid\` refuses the same documents on every door** (2026-11-01): an invoice with an active credit note, a draft included, answers \`400 INVOICE_PAID_NOT_PAYABLE\` with \`details.reason\` \`active_credit_note\`, as the dashboard always has. A delivery note answers the same code with \`details.reason\` \`delivery_note\` (it was \`VALIDATION_ERROR\`). A \`force: true\` past the duplicate guard on a full settlement is recorded in the behandlingshistorik.
- **Behaviour change: \`payment_date\` after today (the Swedish calendar day) answers \`400 PAYMENT_DATE_IN_FUTURE\`** (2026-11-01) on both mark-paid endpoints and the MCP tool, under dry-run too, a credit note refund included. On supplier invoices it was \`VALIDATION_ERROR\`; on customer invoices it was booked.
- **Behaviour change: a signed bank payment stops the credit and the link to an existing verifikat** (2026-11-01): \`POST /supplier-invoices/{id}/credit\` and the MCP tool \`gnubok_link_supplier_invoice_to_voucher\` answer \`409 SI_BANK_PAYMENT_UNDER_WAY\`, as mark-paid does, while a bank payment signed for the invoice will still execute. Cancel that payment first; once the money has left, match its bank row to the invoice instead. That match stays open: the row is that payment.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /transactions/{id}/link-journal-entry\` refuses a row larger than the invoice** (2026-11-01) with \`400 MATCH_AMOUNT_EXCEEDS_REMAINING\`, before anything is written. It used to record the whole row as paid and clamp the remainder at zero.

### Invoices: issuing and credit notes (2026-11)

- **Behaviour change: a momsfri sale is issued like any other** (2026-11-01). \`POST /invoices/{id}/mark-sent\` and \`/send\` answered \`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\` (\`moms_ruta\`) for every invoice of a company outside the VAT register, and the advice to re-create the draft could not help: such a sale has \`vat_treatment=exempt\`, \`vat_amount=0\` and states no \`moms_ruta\`. Every other invoice with no \`moms_ruta\` is still refused, an \`exempt\` one at a VAT-registered company included: send its items with \`PATCH /invoices/{id}\`.
- **Behaviour change: a delivery note is marked sent, never emailed** (2026-11-01). \`POST /invoices/{id}/mark-sent\` issues one (no verifikat, its D-series number kept), as the dashboard does: \`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\` no more. \`POST /invoices/{id}/send\` refuses one with \`400 INVOICE_SEND_DELIVERY_NOTE\` (was \`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\`).
- **Behaviour change: a credit note is a link or a total below zero** (2026-11-01). \`/mark-sent\`, \`/send\`, \`/mark-paid\`, \`/book\` and the match doors treat a draft or open invoice with \`total < 0\` and no \`credited_invoice_id\` (an imported kreditfaktura) as the credit note it is. \`GET /invoices?status=sent\` keeps listing it; it is never reported as overdue.
- **New: \`POST /invoices/{id}/credit\` says it delivered nothing** (2026-11-01). Every response carries warning \`CREDIT_NOTE_NOT_DELIVERED\`: the credit note is issued and booked, and sending its PDF to the customer is yours.
- **Fixed: \`GET /customers/{id}?expand=invoices\` lists what is owed** (2026-11-01): a sent credit note or an invoice with nothing remaining is no longer an open invoice.

### Invoices (2026-10)

- **Behaviour change: \`POST /invoices/{id}/credit\` runs the credit the dashboard and MCP use, and fails closed** (2026-10-13). The credit note now mirrors the original line for line with its revenue accounts, ROT/RUT and periodisering fields and its payee: on a ROT/RUT invoice the reversal credits 1513 for Skatteverket's share and 1510 for the customer's (it credited 1510 for the full total and left 1513 standing), deferred revenue is reversed on its 29xx account and the accrual schedule stops (it reversed 30xx while the schedule kept dissolving), and a line with its own \`revenue_account\` reverses on that account. A self-billed original's credit note is numbered \`KR-<its external number>\` (it was numbered after the original's id). No fiscal period for today now also answers \`400 INVOICE_CREDIT_PERIOD_LOCKED\` (\`details.reason\` \`no_fiscal_period\`) before anything is written. When the reversing entry cannot be posted the request fails with \`500 INVOICE_CREDIT_ISSUE_INCOMPLETE\` (\`details.failure_steps\`), the credit note stays a draft and the original keeps its status; a retry issues the same credit note. \`500 INVOICE_CREDIT_REPAIR_REQUIRED\` means the entry posted and a later step did not finish; retrying completes it. **Before**, the request answered \`201\` with the original already \`credited\` and a \`JOURNAL_ENTRY_NOT_POSTED\` warning. Crediting a credit note answers \`400 INVOICE_CREDIT_NOT_INVOICE\` with \`details.reason\` \`credit_note\` (was \`cannot credit a credit note\`). The only response warning left is \`PDF_ARCHIVE_FAILED\`. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /invoices/{id}/mark-sent\` issues through the dashboard's issue step and fails closed** (2026-10-13). When the invoice's verifikat cannot be posted (no open or a locked period, a required dimension, an account outside the chart) the request fails with the engine's code or \`500 INVOICE_MARK_SENT_BOOK_FAILED\` (\`details.reason\` in Swedish), and the invoice stays a draft and keeps any number already allocated. **Before**, it answered \`200\` with the invoice \`sent\` and a \`JOURNAL_ENTRY_NOT_POSTED\` warning: an issued invoice without its verifikat. A ROT/RUT invoice now books Dr 1510 for the customer's share and Dr 1513 for Skatteverket's (it debited 1510 for the full total), a periodised line books on its 29xx account with an accrual schedule (it booked on 30xx), and the issued PDF is archived as underlag on the verifikat. A verifikat posted but not linked to the invoice answers \`500 INVOICE_MARK_SENT_REPAIR_REQUIRED\` (was the \`JOURNAL_ENTRY_ID_WRITEBACK_FAILED\` warning), and a draft whose customer was deleted \`409 INVOICE_CUSTOMER_MISSING\`. \`warnings\` now carries \`PDF_ARCHIVE_FAILED\`, \`ACCRUAL_SCHEDULES_NOT_CREATED\` or \`DELIVERY_HISTORY_NOT_RECORDED\`. The MCP mark-sent tool also archives the PDF and emits \`invoice.sent\` now. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /invoices/{id}/mark-paid\` books through the dashboard's payment path** (2026-10-13). Under kontantmetoden a ROT/RUT invoice now books Dr 1930 for the customer's share and Dr 1513 for Skatteverket's (it debited 1930 for the full total and booked no 1513), and a line with its own \`revenue_account\` books on that account (it booked on the default 30xx). Custom \`lines\` on a never-booked kontantmetod invoice post as an \`invoice_cash_payment\` voucher. When the invoice update loses a race (\`409 INVOICE_PAID_RACE\`) or fails, the payment voucher just posted is makulerad with a documented gap instead of staying in the ledger. A refusal from the bookkeeping engine (a locked period, say) answers with the engine's code instead of \`INVOICE_PAID_BOOK_FAILED\`. \`invoice.paid\` carries \`paymentAmount\` in the invoice currency for a foreign invoice settled with SEK lines, as on the dashboard. The \`warnings\` field (\`EVENT_EMIT_FAILED\`) is gone from the response; an emit failure is logged. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /invoices/{id}/mark-paid\` accepts a \`partially_paid\` invoice** (2026-10-13) and books its remaining amount, as the dashboard and now the MCP tool do. It used to answer \`400 INVOICE_PAID_NOT_PAYABLE\`. A never-booked kontantmetod invoice that is already part-paid is still refused with \`400 INVOICE_PAID_CASH_PARTIAL_UNSUPPORTED\`. The API version date is unchanged.
- **\`subtotal_sek\`, \`vat_amount_sek\` and \`total_sek\` are stored in whole öre** (2026-10-13) on a foreign-currency invoice created or edited through any door (\`POST /invoices\`, \`PATCH /invoices/{id}\`, \`POST /invoices/bulk-create\`, the dashboard and MCP). They used to hold the raw product of amount and rate (for example \`11235.62345\`). Existing invoices are unchanged; the API version date is unchanged.
- **v1 invoice items carry \`accrual_period_start\`, \`accrual_period_end\` and \`accrual_balance_account\`** (2026-10-13) on create, \`GET /invoices/{id}\`, \`PATCH /invoices/{id}\` and \`:send\`, the periodisering fields \`POST /invoices\` already accepts. **Behaviour change:** \`POST /invoices/{id}/send\` now books a periodised line on its 29xx account with an accrual schedule, as the dashboard does; it used to book it as immediate revenue on 30xx. Additive fields; the API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: \`POST /transactions/{id}/match-invoice\` refuses a kontantmetod payment it cannot book once** (2026-10-13): for an invoice never booked at issue under kontantmetoden, a partial payment and the final payment of an invoice already part-paid both answer \`400 INVOICE_PAID_CASH_PARTIAL_UNSUPPORTED\` (\`details.reason\` \`partial_payment\` or \`previously_partially_paid\`), the code the dashboard and the MCP match already return. **Before**, the partial answered \`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\` (\`details.field\` \`accounting_method\`) and the final payment of a part-paid invoice was booked as the whole invoice, recognising the earlier installments' revenue and moms a second time. Every refusal (this one, unbalanced \`lines\`, an inactive settlement account) now comes before the reversal of the transaction's earlier voucher, so a refused match leaves that voucher in place. The API version date is unchanged.

- **New journal entry \`source_type\` \`rot_rut_reclassification\`** (crm#1144, 2026-10-14): a voucher that moves the ROT, RUT or grön teknik deduction of an invoice imported from Visma from 1510 to 1513 (debit 1513, credit 1510, \`source_id\` the invoice), booked by the post-migration deduction step on the import page. It can appear in journal entry and general ledger responses; like the other engine-owned types it cannot be created through \`POST /journal-entries\` (\`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\`). The invoice then carries \`deduction_total\` and per-row deduction fields like an invoice issued in Accounted. Invoices imported part-paid now read \`partially_paid\` instead of \`sent\`. Additive.

- **Behaviour change: an invoice number is never issued under a higher number of its series, and is unique by value** (2026-10-12): numbering an invoice (\`:send\`, \`:mark-sent\`, \`:send-peppol\`, and the MCP send, mark-sent and convert tools) takes the first free number from \`next_invoice_number\` on, skipping numbers the series already has, and is refused with \`409 INVOICE_NUMBER_SERIES_BEHIND\` when the series already holds a higher number (typically after importing invoices from another system). \`details.first_allowed\` is the lowest next number that continues the series. Nothing is used up: set \`next_invoice_number\` to \`first_allowed\` or higher, or a new \`invoice_prefix\`, with \`PATCH /settings\`, then retry. A settings save that moves \`next_invoice_number\` or \`invoice_prefix\` onto a number the series already has, or under its highest number, is refused with \`400 SETTINGS_INVOICE_NUMBER_IN_SERIES\`. Numbers are compared by value, so \`1\` and \`001\` are the same number: an invoice whose number already exists in another spelling is refused like any taken number. Proformas number from their own \`PF-\` series and no longer leave a hole in the invoice series. **Before**, the number came from the counter alone: a counter set onto an imported number failed with \`INVOICE_SEND_NUMBER_ASSIGN_FAILED\` on every attempt, and a counter below imported invoices issued numbers under them, such as \`001\` next to an imported \`1\`. No field was removed, and the API version date is unchanged.

- **Domestic reverse charge for construction services** (crm#1007, 2026-10-05): \`POST /invoices\` and \`PATCH /invoices/{id}\` accept \`vat_treatment=reverse_charge_domestic\`, omvänd betalningsskyldighet under ML 16 kap. 13 § (the buyer is a construction business and the supply a construction service). The invoice gets 0 % on every line, \`moms_ruta\` 41, revenue on 3231 when sent, and the notice "Omvänd betalningsskyldighet, byggtjänster, ML 16 kap. 13 §" with the buyer's VAT number on the PDF. It needs \`customer_type=swedish_business\` with a Swedish \`vat_number\` (SE + 12 digits) and takes no \`delivery_country\`: \`400 INVOICE_VAT_TREATMENT_DOMESTIC_BUYER_REQUIRED\` (\`details.reason\`) or \`_DELIVERY_COUNTRY_MISMATCH\` otherwise. Additive: nothing changes for a request without it. Not accepted by \`POST /invoices/bulk-create\`.

### Customers (2026-10)

- **Behaviour change: \`default_payment_terms: 0\` is stored as 0** (2026-10-13) on \`POST /customers\`, as on the dashboard and MCP create: 0 days (betalning direkt) used to be replaced by the company's \`invoice_default_days\`, else 30. An omitted value still takes that default. The API version date is unchanged.

### Payroll (2026-10)

- **Behaviour change: \`PATCH /salary/settings\` is for an owner or admin** (2026-11-01). The endpoint writes company settings, which only an owner or admin may change in the app. A member's key was let through; it now gets \`403 FORBIDDEN\` with \`details.required_roles\`, on a dry run too. Reading (\`GET /salary/settings\`) is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: payment files pay from the account the salary is booked on** (crm#1483, 2026-10-26): a pain.001 from \`POST /salary-runs/{id}/payment-file\` and \`POST /supplier-payment-batches\` (and the dashboard's tax file) pays from the cash account the salary verifikat credits: a booked run's verifikat account, otherwise the company's primary bank account. It used to pay from the IBAN in company settings, which is what SEK invoices print and could be another account than the one the salary is booked on. The account's own IBAN is used (the bank-reported one for a connected account, the entered one for a manual account), and its BIC (saved, named by the bank connection, or derived). Settings \`iban\` and \`bic\` remain the fallback when that account has no IBAN and is the company's only SEK bank account, or the company has no bank accounts; otherwise the call is refused with \`422 SALARY_RUN_PAYMENT_FILE_MISSING_BANK_DETAILS\` or \`400 SI_BATCH_DEBTOR_INCOMPLETE\` and \`details.account\` (cash_account_id, name, ledger_account, iban_last4) names the account. New: \`paying_account\` on the salary payment-file response (null for \`bg_lb\`) and \`debtor_account\` on the supplier batch preview. Bankgirot LB files still go from the company bankgiro, and Swedbank's ids stay company settings. \`salary_default_bank\` is still accepted; the dashboard now opens the upload instructions of the paying account's bank and uses it only as a fallback.
- **New: Fora's monthly report** (crm#1389, 2026-10-22): employees take \`fora_fok_id\` (the FOK code from Fora's Mina sidor, \`FOK\` plus six digits) and \`fora_fok_start_date\` on \`POST /employees\` and \`PATCH /employees/{id}\`, set together, never on \`company_owner\` or \`board_member\`; \`GET /employees/{id}\` returns them. \`GET /salary/fora-report?year=&month=\` (scope \`payroll:read\`) answers what the month's Fora file says: each coded worker, the code and the cash gross pay paid out in that payment month in whole kronor (the bruttolön less taxable traktamente and taxable car allowance), plus warnings; personnummer are masked and the file itself is downloaded on the salary run page. 400 \`FORA_REPORT_INCOMPLETE\` lists what blocks the file in \`details.issues\`. Additive.
- **Text rows on the payslip, and behaviour change: a 0 kr line is refused** (crm#1076, 2026-10-14): \`item_type: "text"\` (Textrad) is a new payslip line for words without money, such as how the salary is built up. Add one to a single payslip with \`POST /salary-runs/{id}/employees/{employeeId}/lines\`, or to every payslip with \`POST /employees/{id}/recurring-lines\` (copied into each run like the other recurring lines and printed under the base salary). Send \`description\` (at most 200 characters) and leave out \`amount\`, \`quantity\` and \`unit_price\`; the row is stored with amount 0, every flag false and no account, and never reaches tax, the AGI or the booking. **Behaviour change:** every other line now needs a non-zero amount, from every door (these endpoints, the dashboard and the MCP tools): a 0 kr line, or one without \`amount\`, is refused with \`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\` (\`details.field\` \`amount\`), and so is a \`PATCH /salary-runs/{id}/lines/{lineId}\` that sets a 0 kr amount. The one exception is a \`vacation\` line carrying its days in \`quantity\`. Before, a 0 kr line was accepted and printed "0,00" on the payslip; use a text row instead. A line cannot be changed into or out of a text row (\`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\`, \`details.field\` \`item_type\`): delete it and add a new one. Recurring additions are still refused: a standing raise goes on the employee's \`monthly_salary\`. \`amount\` is now optional in both request bodies; the API version date is unchanged.
- **Förhöjt skatteavdrag per employee** (crm#1073, 2026-10-14): \`POST /employees\` and \`PATCH /employees/{id}\` accept \`extra_tax_amount\` (whole kronor per salary run, 1 to 1 000 000) or \`extra_tax_percentage\` (a requested total, above 0 and at most 100 with two decimals: withhold the higher of the statutory tax and this share of the taxable income), never both (\`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\` on \`extra_tax_percentage\`; send the other as \`null\` in the same PATCH to switch). The employer must honour such a request from the employee's main income (SFL 11 kap. 22 §). A salary run adds the extra after the table or jämkning tax, capped at the cash pay left after that tax and the net deductions; it is not applied with F-skatt, sidoinkomst, an unverified tax status or without a tax table, and the stored value is kept. It is part of \`tax_withheld\`, so the booking, AGI field 001, year-to-date totals and the payment file carry the total, and the payslip PDF prints the extra on its own row (one tax row under a per-run tax override). \`GET /salary-runs/{id}/employees\` adds \`effective.extra_tax_withheld\` and the payslip detail also \`extra_tax_withheld\`: the extra part of the tax, 0 under a per-run tax override. \`GET /employees/{id}\` returns both fields. Additive: nothing changes for an employee without them.
- **Behaviour change: payslip lines carry an account only when one was chosen** (2026-10-14): \`account_number\` on a payslip line is now an override. A line created without one (by \`POST /salary-runs/{id}/employees/{employeeId}/lines\` or by the calculation) returns \`account_number: null\` and books on the default the booking resolves from \`item_type\`, the employee's \`employment_type\` and \`personnel_category\`. Before, the default was written onto the line when it was created, so an owner's hourly or manual line could stay on 7210 and a line whose \`item_type\` changed kept its old account. \`PATCH /salary-runs/{id}/lines/{lineId}\` accepts \`account_number: null\` to drop an override, and a patch that changes \`item_type\` drops a stored account unless it sets one. Lines on runs that were not yet booked had their old defaults cleared the same way; booked runs are unchanged. The API version date is unchanged.
- **New: \`personnel_category\` on employees** (2026-10-14): \`arbetare\` or \`tjansteman\` (the default). An arbetare's wages book on 7010, vacation pay on 7082 and the vacation-liability change on 7090; a tjänsteman's on 7210, 7285 and 7290. Owners and board members keep their own accounts whatever it says. Accepted by \`POST /employees\` and \`PATCH /employees/{id}\` (no null), returned by every employee response, and \`GET /employees?personnel_category=\` filters on it. Unbooked runs follow a change at their booking; a booked run keeps the category it was booked with. \`GET /reports/salary-journal\` rows carry \`personnelCategory\`, and \`groupTotals\` sums the period per category, with owners and board members as their own groups. Additive.
- **Behaviour change: \`personnummer_masked\` reads \`YYYYMMDD-XXXX\`** (2026-10-12) on every employee and salary-run employee response (\`GET /employees\`, \`POST /employees\`, \`PATCH /employees/{id}\`, \`GET /salary-runs/{id}/employees\` and its payslip detail), the form the app, payslips and MCP already showed. It read \`YYYYMMDDXXXX\` (no hyphen). A stored value that is not a 10- or 12-digit number is redacted whole (\`XXXXXXXX-XXXX\`). The detail \`GET /employees/{id}\` still returns the full value. The API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: an omitted \`voucher_series\` on \`POST /salary-runs\` follows the company's salary series** (2026-10-13): the company's voucher series setting for \`salary_payment\` (\`K\` on the standard series set, \`A\` for a company without one), the series the app and MCP book lön into and the systemdokumentation lists. It used to default to \`A\` whatever the company documented. An explicit \`voucher_series\` still wins, and a dry run previews the resolved letter. The run still starts empty. A \`409 SALARY_RUN_DUPLICATE_PERIOD\` now also names the live run (\`details.existing_id\`, \`details.existing_status\`). The API version date is unchanged.
- **New: \`effective\` on \`GET /salary-runs/{id}/employees\` and \`GET /salary-runs/{id}/employees/{employeeId}\`** (2026-10-13): the gross, tax, net, avgifter, vacation accrual and employer cost the booking, the AGI and the bank file use once the review overrides apply, with \`tax_overridden\` and \`avgifter_overridden\`. The pitfalls used to say the effective value is \`COALESCE(override, calculated)\`, which is wrong for the net (a tax override moves the payout too) and for an F-skatt payee's avgifter (the override is ignored). The plain fields are unchanged: they stay the calculation's values. Additive.

### Portfolio and event polling: the multi-user seat gate (2026-10)

- **\`GET /portfolio/overview\` adds \`scope.dormant\`** (2026-10-13): companies paused for the key user by the multi-user seat gate (a non-owner in a company whose multi-user plan lapsed past its grace) are left out of \`companies\` and listed there, as every per-company endpoint already refuses them with \`403\`; a paused company no longer takes one of the 25 scope slots. \`GET /api/events\` answers \`403 FORBIDDEN\` for such a key the same way. The seat gate is off unless the instance turns it on, so nothing changes where it is off. Additive.

### Webhooks (2026-10)

- **New webhook: \`period.lock_date_changed\`** (2026-10-28): fires when the company-wide lock date (\`bookkeeping_locked_through\`, "Bokföring låst t.o.m.", the usual monthly close) is set, moved or removed, through the settings page, \`PATCH /settings/bookkeeping-lock\` or an approved staged change. The payload carries \`previousLockDate\`, \`lockDate\` (\`null\` when the lock was removed), \`direction\` (\`forward\` or \`backward\`), \`via\` (\`app\`, \`api\` or \`approval\`: the door, never the person) and \`reopenedFiledVatPeriods\` (the filed momsdeklaration periods a backward move reopened, empty otherwise). It fires only when the stored date really changes, never on a dry run. Also served by \`GET /api/events\`. Additive; the API version date is unchanged.
- **\`journal_entry.committed\` reaches the event feed in the posting transaction** (2026-10-15): the \`GET /api/events\` row for a posted verifikat is written by the same database transaction that posts it, so it exists exactly when the voucher was posted. Before, it was written after the commit returned, and a request that crashed or timed out in between posted the voucher without the event. The row's \`data\` is unchanged (\`entry\` with its \`lines\`); webhook delivery is unchanged and still queued after the commit. The API version date is unchanged.
- **One webhook can receive several event types** (2026-10-15): \`POST /webhooks\` and \`PATCH /webhooks/{id}\` accept \`event_types\` (one or more event types), and every webhook read returns it. \`event_type\` is still accepted (as a one-entry list) and still returned (the first listed type). \`PATCH\` with \`event_types\` replaces the list, so an existing webhook's events can change without recreating it; \`api_version_pinned\` is kept. Listing \`salary_run.*\` or \`agi.generated\` needs \`payroll:read\`, as before. Each delivery still carries one event. Additive; the API version date is unchanged.
- **The event feed serves every webhook event type** (2026-10-15): \`GET /api/events\` now also returns \`invoice.paid\`, \`supplier_invoice.uncredited\`, \`period.unlocked\`, the four \`reconciliation.*\` events, \`salary_run.created\`, \`salary_run.approved\`, \`salary_run.booked\` and \`agi.generated\`. They were deliverable as webhooks but never written to the feed, so a receiver that missed one could not catch up ([event feed](/docs/api/webhooks#catching-up-the-event-feed)). Payroll events need \`payroll:read\` on the key, as webhook registration does: a key without it does not see them, and naming one in \`types\` answers \`403 INSUFFICIENT_SCOPE\`. Events from before the change are not backfilled. Additive; the API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: personnummer and internal user ids are removed from every webhook payload, at any depth** (2026-10-11): \`personal_number\`, \`personnummer\`, \`deduction_personnummer_encrypted\`, \`deduction_personnummer_last4\`, \`personnummer_encrypted\`, \`personnummer_last4\`, \`user_id\` and \`userId\` no longer appear anywhere in \`data.object\`. Before, only a top-level \`userId\` was dropped, so an \`invoice.created\` delivery carried the invoice's \`user_id\` and ROT/RUT personnummer ciphertext and last four digits, and its \`customer\` row's \`personal_number\` and \`user_id\`. The same projection applies to \`POST /webhook-deliveries/{id}/retry\` (an older delivery is re-minimised before it is sent again) and to \`GET /api/events\`. Nothing else in the payload changed; the API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: \`journal_entry.committed\` fires for bulk-booked bank transactions** (2026-10-07): a samlingsverifikat posted by \`POST /transactions/bulk-book\`, the dashboard bulk booking or an approved agent (MCP) bulk booking now emits \`journal_entry.committed\`, like every other posted voucher. Before, those vouchers were posted without the event. Linking rows to an existing voucher (\`existing_journal_entry_id\`) posts nothing new and still emits no \`journal_entry.committed\`; a dry run emits nothing. The payload and the API version date are unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: \`journal_entry.committed\` fires for samlingsbetalningar, utlägg payouts and kursdifferens vouchers** (2026-10-08): the verifikat posted by \`POST /transactions/{id}/match-batch\` (and its dashboard and agent twins), by an expense payout (\`POST /expense-claims/payouts\`, \`POST /transactions/{id}/match-expense-payout\`), and the kursdifferens verifikat (3960/7960) a link of a foreign-currency invoice or supplier invoice to an existing payment voucher can post, now emit \`journal_entry.committed\`. A link without a kursdifferens posts nothing new and emits no \`journal_entry.committed\`; a dry run emits nothing. SIE imports, their undo and provider migrations stay silent on purpose: they bring in history that was posted elsewhere. The payload and the API version date are unchanged.

### Webhooks: endpoint verification (2026-09)

- **Behaviour change: webhook URLs must pass an ownership handshake before events are delivered** (#3191, 2026-09-29). Accounted POSTs a signed \`webhook.verification\` event whose \`data.object.challenge\` the endpoint returns as \`{"challenge": "..."}\` with a 2xx within 10 seconds ([contract](/docs/api/webhooks#endpoint-verification)). New webhooks start \`pending\` and receive nothing until they pass; a changed \`webhook_url\` starts over. Run the handshake with the new \`POST /webhooks/{id}/verify\` (\`422 WEBHOOK_VERIFICATION_FAILED\` with \`details.reason\` on a failure, \`429\` inside a 10-second cooldown); Accounted also retries on its own.
- **Existing webhooks keep receiving events for 30 days** (\`verification_status: "grace_period"\`, end in \`verification_grace_ends_at\`) while Accounted attempts the handshake daily. A webhook still unverified after that is \`paused\`: nothing is delivered until it passes.
- Every webhook read and write response carries \`verification_status\`, \`verified_at\`, \`verification_grace_ends_at\`, \`verification_attempts\`, \`verification_last_attempt_at\`, \`verification_last_error\` and \`verification_next_attempt_at\`. \`POST /webhooks/{id}/test\` and \`POST /webhook-deliveries/{id}/retry\` answer \`409 WEBHOOK_NOT_VERIFIED\` for \`pending\` and \`paused\` webhooks.

### Invoices (2026-09)

- **Behaviour change: \`invoice.paid\` and \`supplier_invoice.paid\` webhooks** (2026-09-30): both now fire once, when an invoice becomes fully paid, on every path that settles it: \`/mark-paid\`, a bank-transaction match (\`/transactions/{id}/match-invoice\`, \`/match-supplier-invoice\`, the batch match), linking a bank transaction or an invoice to an existing voucher, the Stripe payment sync and the agent (MCP) equivalents. Before, a bank match emitted neither event (only \`*.match_confirmed\` internally), so an invoice paid through the bank never reached subscribers; and \`/mark-paid\` also fired them for a partial payment. A partial payment now fires neither event. The payload is unchanged and the API version date is unchanged.
- **Per-invoice VAT treatment** (#2906, 2026-09-27): \`POST /invoices\` and \`PATCH /invoices/{id}\` accept \`vat_treatment\` (\`standard\` | \`export\` | \`reverse_charge\`) and \`delivery_country\` (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, the country the goods are transported to), so an invoice can state its own supply instead of taking the customer's treatment. A Swedish buyer with goods shipped to Norway is now an export: \`vat_treatment=export\`, \`delivery_country=NO\` gives 0 %, \`moms_ruta\` 36, revenue on 3105 and the export notice. \`reverse_charge\` with a delivery country in another member state is an intra-EU supply of goods (0 %, \`moms_ruta\` 35, revenue on 3108, the Article 138 notice) and needs the customer's VIES-validated VAT number from a member state other than Sweden. \`standard\` is Swedish VAT at the line rates. The treatment is refused, never guessed, when the facts do not support it: \`400 INVOICE_VAT_TREATMENT_DELIVERY_COUNTRY_REQUIRED\`, \`_DELIVERY_COUNTRY_MISMATCH\`, \`_BUYER_VAT_NUMBER_REQUIRED\` or \`_NOT_VAT_REGISTERED\`. The dry run and the invoice detail, create and update responses carry \`vat_treatment_override\` and \`delivery_country\` next to \`vat_treatment\`, \`moms_ruta\` and \`reverse_charge_text\`. Nothing changes for a request without the fields. \`POST /invoices/bulk-create\` refuses them per item. **Behaviour change:** a \`vat_treatment\` key on these bodies used to be dropped silently; a value outside the three is now \`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\`.
- **Behaviour change: Swedish VAT for an EU business established in Sweden** (#2783, 2026-09-20): \`POST /invoices\` and \`PATCH /invoices/{id}\` (when items are replaced) now refuse reverse charge for a customer with \`customer_type=eu_business\` whose \`country\` is \`SE\`, even when its \`vat_number\` is VIES-validated. Such an invoice used to be created at 0 % (\`vat_treatment=reverse_charge\`, ruta 39, with the reverse-charge notice); it is now created with Swedish VAT (\`vat_treatment=standard_25\`, ruta 05, no notice) and lines that omit \`vat_rate\` default to 25 %. This is the rule the dashboard, the MCP tools and \`POST /invoices/bulk-create\` already applied, and the one this page has described since the entry below: the two single-invoice routes never read the customer's country, so the same customer got 0 % here and 25 % everywhere else. A buyer established in Sweden owes Swedish VAT whatever foreign VAT number it holds (ML 6 kap. 34 §: a B2B service is taxed where the buyer is established, so reverse charge exists only when that is another member state). The response says why: \`meta.warnings\` carries \`EU_BUSINESS_COUNTRY_IS_SE\` with \`message_sv\`, \`message_en\` and a \`remediation\`, on the live call and on a dry run. Nothing is refused and no status code changed. **If you relied on the old result**, the customer row is what to fix: set \`country\` to where the buyer is actually established (\`PATCH /customers/{id}\`), or change \`customer_type\` to \`swedish_business\` if it is Swedish. A genuinely foreign customer with a validated number is unaffected and still gets reverse charge. Replacing the items of an existing draft re-decides the treatment from the customer's current row, so a draft created at 0 % under the old behaviour moves to Swedish VAT the next time its items are replaced. Invoices already sent are not touched.
- **VAT-treatment warnings** (#2749, #2558, 2026-09-20): \`POST /invoices\`, \`PATCH /invoices/{id}\` (when items are replaced) and \`POST /invoices/bulk-create\` (per item) now say why the VAT treatment is what it is, without changing it. Reverse charge (0 %, ruta 39) needs \`customer_type=eu_business\`, a VIES-validated \`vat_number\` and a country other than SE; when one of those is missing the draft gets Swedish VAT as before and the response carries \`meta.warnings\` (\`EU_BUSINESS_VAT_NUMBER_NOT_VALIDATED\`, \`EU_BUSINESS_VAT_NUMBER_MISSING\`, \`EU_BUSINESS_COUNTRY_IS_SE\`), each with \`message_sv\`, \`message_en\` and a \`remediation\`. A Swedish rate set explicitly on a line to a validated EU or non-EU business is still accepted (the ML 6 kap. supplies taxed where they are performed) but flagged as \`SWEDISH_VAT_TO_REVERSE_CHARGE_CUSTOMER\` / \`SWEDISH_VAT_TO_EXPORT_CUSTOMER\`. Warnings never fail a request; dry runs return the same list. \`meta.warnings\` is a new optional field on every envelope, absent when there is nothing to say.

### Transactions (2026-09)

- **Behaviour change: double-booking guards on categorize** (2026-09-30): \`POST /transactions/{id}/categorize\` and \`POST /transactions/batch-categorize\` now run the two checks the dashboard already ran, on the live call and on a dry run, whenever the transaction has no verifikat yet. A bank line the ledger already books (a booked sibling transaction, or a verifikat booking the same amount on the bank account, such as a supplier invoice marked paid) is refused with \`409 TRANSACTION_BOOK_POSSIBLE_DUPLICATE\` and the candidate in \`details.candidate\`. Link the transaction to that verifikat instead; only for a genuinely separate event, resend with \`force: true\` plus \`expected_duplicate_journal_entry_id\` (or \`expected_duplicate_transaction_id\`) echoing the candidate, which the live call logs in behandlingshistorik. A stale id returns \`409 TRANSACTION_BOOK_FORCE_CANDIDATE_MISMATCH\`. A plain 244x or 151x categorization that an open supplier or customer invoice covers is refused with \`409 TX_CATEGORIZE_SUGGEST_SI_MATCH\` / \`TX_CATEGORIZE_SUGGEST_CI_MATCH\`: match the invoice with \`/match-supplier-invoice\` / \`/match-invoice\`, or pass \`confirm_no_match: true\` to keep the categorization. In \`batch-categorize\` each refusal is a per-item error and the other items still book; an item is never compared with a verifikat booked earlier in the same batch. **Before**, both routes accepted \`force\`, \`expected_duplicate_*\` and \`confirm_no_match\` but never ran the checks, so one bank payment could be booked twice. No field was added or removed, and the API version date is unchanged.
- **Behaviour change: the supplier-invoice bank match books like the dashboard** (#3253, 2026-09-30): \`POST /transactions/{id}/match-supplier-invoice\` now plans and books the payment with the same code as the dashboard match, so the same bank row gives the same verifikat (line texts included) and the same ledger update on both. A same-currency row that pays more than the invoice's remaining balance settles the invoice in full: 2440 is cleared by the remaining balance only and the excess, up to 5 000 kr, is booked on 6570 as a bank fee, under both accounting methods. A SEK row less than 1 kr off the remaining balance of a SEK invoice (a whole-krona payment of an öre total) now settles it in full under faktureringsmetoden too, with the difference on 3740; it used to leave the invoice \`partially_paid\` with the öre on 2440. \`paid_amount\`, \`remaining_amount\` and the payment row record the debt settled and never exceed the invoice total. A same-currency excess above the fee cap is refused with \`400 MATCH_SI_AMOUNT_EXCEEDS_REMAINING\` and books nothing; it used to clear the whole bank amount off 2440 and push \`paid_amount\` past the total. Allocate such a payment across invoices with \`POST /transactions/{id}/match-batch\`. A cross-currency match is not capped, as before: it settles the remaining balance and books the SEK difference as kursdifferens. The plan's refusals (the overshoot, a kontantmetoden partial, a missing exchange rate) and the check that custom \`lines\` balance now run before a conflicting categorization of the transaction is reversed; they used to run after it, so a refused request left the reversal posted. The response gains \`bank_fee_sek\`, the SEK booked on 6570 (0 when there is none, and with custom \`lines\`). The request shape is unchanged.

### Customers (2026-09)

- **Sole traders (enskild firma)** (#2367, 2026-09-13): an \`org_number\` shaped like a Swedish personnummer is now accepted on \`customer_type=swedish_business\`. A sole trader has no separate organisationsnummer: its owner's personnummer IS the firm's org number, so the old blanket \`400 CUSTOMER_ORG_NUMBER_IS_PERSONAL\` made a real customer impossible to register as a business. The refusal now applies to \`eu_business\` and \`non_eu_business\` only, where the value cannot be an org number at all; \`individual\` is unchanged (a personnummer there is still moved into \`personal_number\`). The data-minimisation reason behind the old rule moved to the read paths where it belongs: \`GET /customers\` returns \`org_number\` and \`vat_number\` as \`null\` for any row whose \`org_number\` is a personnummer, the masking individual rows already had. \`GET /customers/{id}\` still returns the full value.

### Chart of accounts (2026-09)

- **Order** (2026-09-11): \`GET /accounts\` returns accounts in \`account_number\` order, the BAS sequence it always documented. It used to sort by the stored \`sort_order\`, which is \`0\` on every account seeded at company creation, so the seeded accounts came first and the rest followed.
- **Class filter**: \`?class\` accepts any digit \`0\`-\`9\`, the first digit of \`account_number\`. Class \`9\` appears on internal accounts carried over from an imported chart and could not be filtered on before.
- **Schema**: the response schema lists the \`account_type\` values (\`untaxed_reserves\` included), \`normal_balance\` and \`default_vat_treatment\`. No field was added or removed, and the API version date is unchanged.
- **Journal entry dry runs**: \`POST /journal-entries?dry_run=true\` now resolves the lines' accounts against the chart and fails with \`400 ACCOUNTS_NOT_IN_CHART\` for a deactivated account or a non-BAS number the chart does not contain, the same verdict as the live call. A standard BAS account that is not in the chart yet still passes: the live call adds it.

### OpenAPI spec and reference pages (2026-09)

- **Query parameters in the spec**: \`/api/v1/openapi.json\` now lists every endpoint's query parameters (filters, pagination \`cursor\` / \`limit\`, report \`period_id\` and date ranges, \`expand\`) with type, requiredness and description, and \`dry_run\` on every dry-run-capable endpoint. Before, the spec carried path parameters only.
- **Nullable fields**: nullable fields are published as \`type: [T, "null"]\` (OpenAPI 3.1). Before, they read as non-null, so a strict generated client could reject a valid response.
- **Reference pages**: each endpoint section shows its query parameters, request body fields and response fields. New pages: Bank accounts (\`/cash-accounts\`, \`/bank-connections\`), Skatteverket (filed VAT declarations) and Health; company settings are on Companies, vacation-year close on Salary runs.
- Documentation only: no request or response changed, and the API version date is unchanged.

### Reports and journal entries: dimensions (2026-09)

- **Line dimensions on journal-entry reads** (2026-09-28): \`GET /journal-entries/{id}\` and the \`POST /journal-entries\` response carry each line's \`dimensions\` (\`{"<dim_no>": "<code>"}\`, \`{}\` when untagged), so dimension 2, 7-9 and custom dimensions 20+ are visible; \`cost_center\` and \`project\` stay as mirrors of keys \`1\` and \`6\`. The dry-run preview echoes the bag the engine stores. \`PATCH /journal-entries/{id}\` (draft edit) answers \`dimensions\` on every line.
- **Dimension filter on reports** (2026-09-28): \`GET /reports/income-statement\`, \`/reports/general-ledger\` and \`/reports/monthly-breakdown\` accept \`dim_no\` + \`dim_code\` (together) and then answer \`dimension_filter\` and \`partial_view\` (\`complete: false\`; on the general ledger \`opening_balances_included: false\`, every \`opening_balance\` is 0 under a filter). The trial balance and the statutory reports refuse the pair.
- **Fix: project opening balances on the filtered general ledger** (2026-10-01): under \`dim_no\` + \`dim_code\` the general ledger's \`opening_balance\` was always 0, so a project's work in progress or receivable carried from last year read as zero. It is now that value's own IB: the IB lines tagged with it, or, when the year has no IB entry, its prior tagged history. The year-end close and the SIE import (\`#OIB\`) now split each balance-sheet account's IB per project (dimension 6), except the VAT accounts (26xx), whose IB stays one untagged line. Under a filter, dimensions that reset annually (kostnadsställe, dimension 1, and custom dimensions by default) and the 26xx accounts open at 0. \`partial_view\` now carries \`opening_balances: "dimension_scoped"\`, and \`opening_balances_included\` stays in the body but is \`true\` (it was \`false\`). Unfiltered reports are unchanged. A bug fix: the API version date is unchanged.
- **Split an existing IB per project** (#3313, 2026-10-03, additive): \`GET /fiscal-periods/{id}/opening-balances/split-per-project\` previews splitting the year's IB verifikat per project from the previous year's closing balances per object of the dimensions that carry across years (projekt, dimension 6): per balance-sheet account the current and the proposed lines (one per project plus an untagged remainder; the account total never changes), which accounts change, project codes missing from the registry, and \`blocked\` when the year does not allow it. \`POST\` on the same path applies it as an inline rättelse of the same verifikat (the struck lines stay in the rättelse log); pass the preview's \`fingerprint\` as \`expected_fingerprint\` (\`409 OB_SPLIT_PROPOSAL_CHANGED\` when it moved). Open, unlocked years without a bokslut only: \`409 OB_SPLIT_PERIOD_CLOSED\`, \`OB_SPLIT_PERIOD_LOCKED\`, \`OB_COMPANY_LOCK_DATE\`, \`OB_CORRECT_YEAR_END_EXISTS\`. A split already in place answers \`applied: false\` (its \`?dry_run=true\` answers \`409 OB_SPLIT_NOTHING_TO_DO\`, so nothing is staged), and an account whose IB already carries a different project split, for example from SIE \`#OIB\`, is skipped (\`skip_reason: "existing_split"\`), never overwritten. The preview's \`changed_amount_sek\` is what an API key's unattended-commit ceiling prices. MCP: \`gnubok_preview_opening_balance_split\` and the staged \`gnubok_split_opening_balances_per_project\`.
- **Behaviour change, dimension filters only:** every \`GET /reports/*\` endpoint and the årsredovisning reads under \`/fiscal-periods/{id}/arsredovisning\` answer \`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\` (\`unknown_params\` + \`allowed_params\` in details) to a dimension filter they do not document (\`dim_no\`, \`dim_code\`, \`dimensions\`, \`project\`, \`cost_center\`). Before, they silently ignored it, so \`dim_no\` on the trial balance returned the unfiltered report as if it were filtered.
- **Ignored parameters are named** (2026-09-28): any other query parameter a report does not document is still not applied and not refused; the response now names it in the \`X-Ignored-Query-Params\` header (comma-separated). Check it when a filter seems to have had no effect. If these are ever refused too, that change will be announced here first.

### Reconciliation, account-keyed (2026-08)

- **Accounts**: \`GET /reconciliation/accounts\` lists every account with an outside truth (bank accounts as \`bank:<cash_account_id>\`, the skattekonto as \`skattekonto\`) with status; \`GET .../accounts/{accountKey}\` is the bridge (outside balance, ledger, difference, unexplained, explanatory lines, counts, latest sign-off); \`GET .../accounts/{accountKey}/items\` the rows behind it, bucketed (proposed, unmatched_external, unmatched_ledger, matched, ignored, upcoming).
- **Links**: \`POST .../accounts/{accountKey}/links\` (pairs or \`use_proposals\`), \`DELETE .../links/{linkId}\`, \`POST .../items/{itemId}/ignore\`. Links never touch the ledger.
- **Verifikat settled against each other** (crm#1074, 2026-10-11, additive): on a bank account in SEK a \`POST .../links\` pair may carry no \`external_ids\` and two or more \`journal_entry_ids\`: verifikat without a bank row whose lines on the account sum to exactly zero (a wrong verifikat and the correction booked by hand). They leave \`unmatched_ledger\` together and come back in the new \`settled[]\` with a \`settlement_id\`; the items endpoint lists them under \`matched\` with a \`settlement\` object, and \`DELETE .../links/{settlement_id}\` undoes it. \`external_ids\` is now optional in the request and every links response carries \`settled\` (empty unless such a pair was sent). New skip codes \`ENTRY_NOT_OPEN\` and \`ALREADY_SETTLED\`. \`GET /reconciliation/bank/status\` gains \`settled_gl_entry_count\` and \`settled_gl_line_total\`, and the bridge a \`settled_ledger\` line, for a settled verifikat whose counterpart is dated outside the window; \`unexplained_difference\` is the same before and after a settlement. Nothing is proposed for this shape and \`use_proposals\` never applies it.
- **Sign-off**: \`POST .../accounts/{accountKey}/signoff\` ("avstämt t.o.m." a date; refused with an unexplained difference unless forced with a note), \`GET .../signoff\` history, \`POST .../signoff/{signoffId}/reopen\`.
- New scopes \`reconciliation:read\`, \`reconciliation:write\`, \`reconciliation:signoff\`. The legacy \`/reconciliation/bank/*\` endpoints and their \`transactions:*\` scopes are unchanged.
- **Webhooks**: new event types \`reconciliation.matched\`, \`reconciliation.unmatched\`, \`reconciliation.signed_off\`, \`reconciliation.reopened\`. Additive: existing subscriptions are unaffected and the API version date is unchanged.

### Reports, companies, Skatteverket, customers, transactions (2026-08, additive)

Backfilled 2026-08-26 from merged PRs. Every item is additive (new endpoints, optional fields, optional filters): the API version date stays \`${API_V1_VERSION}\`.

- **Custom date ranges on reports** (#1909, 2026-08-25): \`GET /reports/income-statement\` accepts optional \`from_date\` / \`to_date\` (\`YYYY-MM-DD\`, both inside the fiscal period named by \`period_id\`, \`from_date <= to_date\`). \`GET /reports/balance-sheet\` is a position, so it takes only \`to_date\` (or its alias \`as_of\`) and refuses \`from_date\`. Omit them for the whole period, as before. These routes now reject unknown query parameters with \`400 VALIDATION_ERROR\` (\`unknown_params\` + \`allowed_params\` in details) instead of silently returning a full-period report.
- **Report PDFs** (#1909): \`GET /reports/balance-sheet/pdf\` and \`GET /reports/income-statement/pdf\` return \`application/pdf\`, byte-equivalent to the dashboard export, with the same \`period_id\` and range parameters. Scope \`reports:read\`.
- **Company creation** (#1864, 2026-08-25): \`POST /api/v1/companies\` (scope \`companies:write\`) creates a company and sets it up in one call: owner membership, BAS chart of accounts for the company form, compliance settings, the first fiscal period and the automatic tax deadlines. A VAT-registered company must send \`moms_period\`. (Since 2026-10-15 it requires and replays \`Idempotency-Key\`: see Retries above.)
- **Filed VAT declarations** (#1773, 2026-08-21): \`GET /skatteverket/vat-declarations?period_type=&year=&period=\` (scope \`compliance:read\`) reads one period's momsdeklaration as Skatteverket has it on file: \`submitted\` (SKV inlämnat) and \`decided\` (SKV beslutat), each \`null\` when nothing is on file. Live read, requires an active Skatteverket connection on the company.
- **Company settings write** (#1405, 2026-08-04): \`PATCH /companies/{companyId}/settings\` (scope \`companies:write\`, risk medium, dry-run supported) updates bank details (\`bank_name\`, \`clearing_number\`, \`account_number\`, \`bankgiro\`, \`plusgiro\`, \`swish\`, \`iban\`, \`bic\`), \`contact_person\`, \`email\`, \`phone\`, \`website\` and \`invoice_email_texts\`, with the same validation as the MCP tool.
- **Customer \`personal_number\`** (#1724 2026-08-20, #1788 2026-08-21): \`personal_number\` on customer create, bulk-create, detail, PATCH and list. Accepted only for \`customer_type=individual\`, stored encrypted, always returned masked (\`********-1234\`); sending the masked form on PATCH means "leave unchanged", \`null\` clears it. A personnummer-shaped \`org_number\` on a business customer type is refused (\`400 CUSTOMER_ORG_NUMBER_IS_PERSONAL\`); on an individual it is moved into \`personal_number\` and \`org_number\` is cleared, or refused with \`400 CUSTOMER_PERSONAL_NUMBER_CONFLICT\` when it differs from a \`personal_number\` in the same body.
- **Ignore a transaction** (#1661, 2026-08-29): \`POST /transactions/{id}/ignore\` (scope \`transactions:write\`, risk low, idempotent, dry-run supported) marks an unbooked bank transaction as ignored without writing a verifikat, so it is allowed in a locked or closed period: the path for rows that are not business events (PSD2 ghost rows, duplicates, transfers that never executed). \`DELETE\` on the same path restores the row. A booked transaction (directly, via a payment allocation, or via a voucher link) is refused with \`409 TX_IGNORE_ALREADY_BOOKED\`. In the same change, \`/categorize\` and \`/batch-categorize\` answer \`is_business: false\` in a locked period with \`400 TX_CATEGORIZE_PRIVATE_PERIOD_LOCKED\` (\`details.suggested_action: "ignore"\`) instead of a bare \`PERIOD_LOCKED\`: a private marking is a real eget uttag / insättning booking, so the lock still applies to it.
- **Transactions by bank account** (#1809, 2026-08-23): transaction list and detail carry \`cash_account_id\`; \`GET /transactions?cash_account_id=<uuid>\` filters to one bank account.

### Bookkeeping primitives + AP + compliance (Phase 4)

- **Suppliers + supplier-invoices** vertical (mirror of Phase 2 invoices on the AP side).
- **Journal entries** primitives: \`POST /journal-entries\` (draft+commit), \`/{id}/commit\`, \`/{id}/reverse\` (storno) and \`/{id}/correct\` (rättelse): both satisfy BFL 5 kap 5 § (storno is the canonical method of rättelse), \`/batch-create\`.
- **Voucher gap explanations**: \`POST /voucher-gap-explanations\` per BFNAR 2013:2.
- **Fiscal-periods ops**: \`/lock\`, \`/close\` and \`/opening-balances\` are synchronous and return 200 with the updated period; \`/year-end\` and \`/currency-revaluation\` are async and return 202 with operation_id (poll at \`GET /api/v1/operations/{id}\`).
- **Compliance check**: \`GET /compliance/check?type={year_end_readiness|voucher_gaps}\`: pre-flight findings before submission.
- **Documents**: \`POST /documents\` (multipart upload, magic-number-checked), \`GET /{id}/download\` (15-min signed URL), \`POST /{id}/link\` (attach to journal entry).

### Payroll + reports + import (Phase 5)

- **Employees**: full CRUD with personnummer masking on list/create per GDPR Art.5(1)(c). Soft-delete via \`is_active\`.
- **Salary runs**: CRUD + lifecycle verbs \`/calculate\`, \`/approve\`, \`/mark-paid\`, \`/book\`, \`/generate-agi\`. State machine: draft → review → approved → paid → booked. \`/generate-agi\` produces and persists the arbetsgivardeklaration XML: the response carries it as \`data.xml\` for the integrator to upload to Skatteverket Mina Sidor (or via the optional \`skatteverket\` extension). Accounted does NOT auto-submit; the AGI deadline: **the 12th of the following month for every reporting period EXCEPT January and August, where companies with annual turnover ≤ 40 MSEK get the 17th**: is the integrator's responsibility.
- **JSON reports** (13): trial-balance, balance-sheet, income-statement, general-ledger, journal-register, vat-declaration, monthly-breakdown, ar-ledger, supplier-ledger, continuity-check, salary-journal, avgifter-basis, vacation-liability.
- **Binary report**: \`GET /reports/sie-export\` (text/plain SIE4 file). Note: a SIE4 export alone does NOT satisfy BFL 7 kap archiving obligations: SIE captures account-level positions and verifikationer but lacks system documentation and behandlingshistorik. Treat SIE as a portability format (Fortnox/Visma/Bokio migration), not as a complete archive.
- **Async imports**: \`POST /imports/sie\` (multipart, 50 MB), \`POST /imports/bank\` (multipart, 10 MB, auto-format detection across 12 bank formats). Both async via \`operations\` substrate. **Post-SIE-import warning:** SIE files do NOT carry VAT codes or tax-rate-to-account mappings, AND they do NOT transfer behandlingshistorik (the source system's processing log required by BFNAR 2013:2 kap 8 §) or systemdokumentation. After importing from Fortnox / Visma / BL / SpeedLedger / Bokio you MUST manually reconfigure VAT codes (typically via \`/settings/tax-codes\`) before the first momsdeklaration; skipping this step is the most common source of incorrect VAT submissions in migrated bookkeeping. The behandlingshistorik gap must be preserved separately: under BFNAR 2013:2 kap 8 § the obligation attaches to the entire räkenskapsår, not from the import date forward. Best practice for a mid-year migration: export the source system's behandlingshistorik for the full fiscal year and archive it alongside the SIE file. Accounted starts a fresh behandlingshistorik from the import date forward; the pre-import portion of the year remains the source system's record.

### 2026-05-15: Webhooks (Phase 6 PR-1)

- **Subscriptions**: \`POST /webhooks\` (HMAC secret returned exactly once), GET list + detail, PATCH, DELETE. Per-event-type elevated scope check (\`salary_run.*\` and \`agi.generated\` require \`payroll:read\`).
- **Delivery substrate**: dispatched immediately after the event is enqueued, with a per-minute Vercel cron at \`/api/webhooks/dispatch/cron\` as the retry and sweep path. Due rows are claimed atomically via the \`claim_due_webhook_deliveries\` SQL function (\`FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED\`), with \`*.pg.test.ts\` coverage for the claim path and the webhook DB triggers. Exponential backoff \`1m / 5m / 30m / 2h / 12h / 24h / 48h\` (7 retries, ~87h total). HTTP 410 from receiver auto-disables the webhook.
- **Signature**: \`X-Gnubok-Signature: t=<unix>,v1=<hex-HMAC-SHA256>\`. Stripe-format. Sample receivers in [Node + Python](/docs/api/webhooks#verifying-signatures).
- **SSRF protection**: webhook_url must be HTTPS; resolved IPs in private/loopback/link-local/CGNAT/cloud-metadata ranges are rejected at create AND dispatch time. Dispatch pins the validated IP through a DNS-rebinding-safe \`node:https.request\` agent (\`lib/webhooks/pinned-fetch.ts\`); redirects are refused on every outbound POST (any 3xx is treated as a blocked redirect).
- **Audit + retention**: webhook delivery rows are *behandlingshistorik* per BFNAR 2013:2 kap 8 §: immutable once terminal so the audit trail of what an integration was notified of stays intact. Delivery rows are NOT räkenskapsinformation themselves; the 7-year statutory retention under BFL 7 kap 1 § applies only to the underlying verifikation / faktura / AGI XML in its own table, NOT to the delivery envelope. Accounted keeps accounting-event delivery rows for 7 years as a voluntary operational policy (the duration aligns with BFL 7 kap on the underlying records but is not itself a statutory obligation on delivery rows). Webhook DELETE preserves the delivery audit trail (\`ON DELETE SET NULL\` on \`webhook_id\`). Webhook lifecycle events (create / update / delete, plus dispatcher auto-disable) each write a V16 \`audit_log\` entry.
- **Verbs**: \`POST /webhooks/{id}/test\` enqueues a synthetic event; \`POST /webhook-deliveries/{id}/retry\` re-enqueues a dead/delivered delivery.

### Coming soon (Phase 6 PR-2 hardening)

- 90-day TTL cleanup cron for non-accounting webhook deliveries
- Per-route rate limits on \`:test\`, \`:retry\`, and webhook \`:create\`
- Populated \`previous_attributes\` for update-style webhook events
`
